{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014eCWLTH9hvqhrKBAH5mQRw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"siglip_projector_rsa\": 0.615,\n7\t      \"trained_with_inst_rsa\": 0.488,\n8\t      \"untrained_with_inst_rsa\": 0.485,\n9\t      \"dino_rsa\": 0.388,\n10\t      \"llm_degradation_delta\": 0.127\n11\t    },\n12\t    \"tables\": [\n13\t      {\n14\t        \"title\": \"SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\",\n15\t        \"columns\": [\n16\t          \"Source\",\n17\t          \"RSA\",\n18\t          \"Architecture Coverage\",\n19\t          \"Worst Interpretation\"\n20\t        ],\n21\t        \"rows\": [\n22\t          [\n23\t            \"SigLIP+Proj\",\n24\t            \"0.615\",\n25\t            \"OpenVLA only\",\n26\t            \"Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\"\n27\t          ],\n28\t          [\n29\t            \"VLA trained\",\n30\t            \"0.488\",\n31\t            \"OpenVLA only\",\n32\t            \"Llama-2-specific LLM degradation\"\n33\t          ],\n34\t          [\n35\t            \"VLA untrained\",\n36\t            \"0.485\",\n37\t            \"OpenVLA only\",\n38\t            \"Random-init Llama-2 specific\"\n39\t          ],\n40\t          [\n41\t            \"DINO\",\n42\t            \"0.388\",\n43\t            \"Standalone\",\n44\t            \"Reference baseline, unaffected\"\n45\t          ]\n46\t        ]\n47\t      }\n48\t    ],\n49\t    \"figures\": [],\n50\t    \"analysis\": \"Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。价值在于 demonstrate\\nframework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——\\nneutral contribution in worst tier。但 LLM degradation finding 可能被用来攻击论文 motivation 本身。\\n\\n\\n数据已完成不变。在 worst 档下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP encoder。Reviewer 攻击路线：\\n\\\"SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific frozen encoder 的观察。TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision encoder，\\nNORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。单架构 encoder analysis 无法 claim architecture-independent。\\\"\\nLLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身被视为 \\\"trivially expected—— LLM 的 intermediate processing 当然会\\n改变 representation geometry，这不是 finding 而是 definition。\\\" 在 diagnostic framework reframe 下，\\n此实验降为 \\\"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的 case study\\\"——不再是 core contribution。更致命的是，Reviewer 会用\\n这个实验反过来攻击论文 motivation：\\\"如果 frozen encoder 已经提供了最好的 action-relevant structure（RSA=0.615），\\n而 LLM processing 只是 degrade 它（到 0.488），那为什么要研究 LLM 内部的 instruction routing？问题不在 routing\\n而在 LLM 设计本身——你应该研究如何让 LLM 不 degrade encoder output。\\\"\\n\"\n51\t  },\n52\t  {\n53\t    \"name\": \"DINO baseline RSA\",\n54\t    \"description\": \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\",\n55\t    \"results\": {\n56\t      \"dino_rsa\": 0.388,\n57\t      \"dino_action_R2\": 0.687,\n58\t      \"dino_subtask_auc\": 0.972\n59\t    },\n60\t    \"tables\": [],\n61\t    \"figures\": [],\n62\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 下 DINO baseline 被用来论证整篇论文的 premise 可疑：如果 vision alone 足够好，\\ninstruction routing research 的 practical relevance 被严重削弱。Framework reframe 可以\\nacknowledge 但无法完全化解这个攻击。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色被 weaponize：R²=0.687 对比 VLA 训练后的 exit R² drop。Reviewer：\\n\\\"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training）的 action probe R²=0.687 已经很高，\\n说明 action prediction 主要是 visual task。你们声称的 VLA 训练重组 instruction routing，但如果一个\\n纯视觉模型无需任何 instruction 就能达到 R²=0.687，instruction routing 的 practical value 是什么？\\n这反而证明了 Grant et al. 2026 的 visual dominance finding——instructions 在 VLA 中可能根本不重要。\\\"\\nDINO subtask AUC=0.972 进一步强化这个论点——task progress 几乎完全可从 visual features 预测，\\n无需 instruction information。这直接攻击论文研究 instruction routing 的 premise。\\n\"\n63\t  },\n64\t  {\n65\t    \"name\": \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\",\n66\t    \"description\": \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\",\n67\t    \"results\": {\n68\t      \"proj_rsa\": 0.615,\n69\t      \"trained_peak_rsa\": 0.488,\n70\t      \"trained_peak_layer\": 9,\n71\t      \"untrained_peak_rsa\": 0.485,\n72\t      \"untrained_peak_layer\": 12,\n73\t      \"proj_to_l1_drop\": 0.13,\n74\t      \"inverted_u_trained\": true,\n75\t      \"inverted_u_untrained\": true,\n76\t      \"rise_phase_delta\": 0.016\n77\t    },\n78\t    \"tables\": [\n79\t      {\n80\t        \"title\": \"RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\",\n81\t        \"columns\": [\n82\t          \"Architecture\",\n83\t          \"RSA Per-Layer Done?\",\n84\t          \"Pattern\",\n85\t          \"Worst Interpretation\"\n86\t        ],\n87\t        \"rows\": [\n88\t          [\n89\t            \"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\",\n90\t            \"Yes\",\n91\t            \"Inverted-U\",\n92\t            \"Only confirmed case, CKA reversal undermines\"\n93\t          ],\n94\t          [\n95\t            \"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\",\n96\t            \"No\",\n97\t            \"Unknown\",\n98\t            \"Cannot claim generalization\"\n99\t          ],\n100\t          [\n101\t            \"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\",\n102\t            \"No\",\n103\t            \"Unknown\",\n104\t            \"Cannot claim generalization\"\n105\t          ]\n106\t        ]\n107\t      }\n108\t    ],\n109\t    \"figures\": [],\n110\t    \"analysis\": \"Inverted-U 成为 C3 observation 的核心证据但被 metric-dependence 严重削弱。\\nFramework reframe 下可保留为 \\\"framework reveals metric-dependent patterns\\\"\\n但这同时 undermine 了 framework 发现的 authority——如果换个 metric 结论就变，framework 的可靠性如何？\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下 inverted-U 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证过，TracVLA/NORA 的 RSA per-layer\\ncurve 从未做过。CKA 在 plan_009 中反转了 RSA ordering（untrained > trained），使 RSA metric 的\\nauthority 受损。Rise phase Δρ=0.016 极小（CI 可能 includes 0），reviewer 会指出：\\n\\\"你声称 training shifts RSA peak from L0 to L12，但 rise phase 只有 0.016 ρ——这在 noise level 内。\\n如果 CKA 不支持 inverted-U，你不能 claim 这是 robust pattern——这是 metric-specific artifact。\\\"\\n在 CoRL（robotics venue），per-layer RSA curve 被视为 \\\"interesting visualization but not\\ncontribution\\\"——reviewer 期望功能性验证而非几何观察。\\n\"\n111\t  },\n112\t  {\n113\t    \"name\": \"Output head analysis\",\n114\t    \"description\": \"SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\",\n115\t    \"results\": {\n116\t      \"vision_projector_cos_sim\": 1.0,\n117\t      \"llm_rel_change_mean\": 1.316,\n118\t      \"llm_rel_change_range\": [\n119\t        1.22,\n120\t        1.37\n121\t      ],\n122\t      \"head_vs_llm_ratio\": 1.12,\n123\t      \"shallow_adaptation_gate\": \"FAIL\"\n124\t    },\n125\t    \"tables\": [],\n126\t    \"figures\": [],\n127\t    \"analysis\": \"贡献接近零。Framework reframe 下可作为 \\\"component attribution capability\\\" 的 one-sentence\\nmention。不值得独立分析。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下此实验被视为 trivial verification：\\\"OpenVLA 代码 freeze 了 vision encoder，\\n你只是验证了代码做了它该做的事。cos_sim=1.0 不是 finding，是 implementation check。\\\"\\nLLM 权重均匀分布（1.22-1.37）也不 surprising——\\\"random init vs pretrained 的差异当然大且均匀，\\n这是 comparing random weights to structured weights，不是 analyzing fine-tuning effects。\\n你的 caveat 自己也说了：comparison is pretrained Llama + fine-tune vs random init，\\n所以 differences dominated by pretrained vs random，not by VLA training.\\\"\\n在 8-page limit 下，worst tier 建议此实验压缩为半段或移到 appendix。\\n\"\n128\t  },\n129\t  {\n130\t    \"name\": \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\",\n131\t    \"description\": \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\",\n132\t    \"results\": {\n133\t      \"trained_untrained_rsa_delta\": 0.003,\n134\t      \"trained_untrained_r2_delta\": 0.015,\n135\t      \"cka_ordering_reversal\": true,\n136\t      \"all_methods_show_vla_gt_dino\": true\n137\t    },\n138\t    \"tables\": [\n139\t      {\n140\t        \"title\": \"6 Methods Under Worst-Tier Reinterpretation\",\n141\t        \"columns\": [\n142\t          \"Method\",\n143\t          \"Trained-Untrained Δ\",\n144\t          \"Worst Reviewer Reading\"\n145\t        ],\n146\t        \"rows\": [\n147\t          [\n148\t            \"RSA (geometric)\",\n149\t            \"0.003\",\n150\t            \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"\n151\t          ],\n152\t          [\n153\t            \"R² action probe\",\n154\t            \"+0.015\",\n155\t            \"Marginal: within noise\"\n156\t          ],\n157\t          [\n158\t            \"CKA (global)\",\n159\t            \"-0.006\",\n160\t            \"REVERSAL: undermines RSA narrative\"\n161\t          ],\n162\t          [\n163\t            \"Action probe (MLP)\",\n164\t            \"+0.045\",\n165\t            \"Small routing effect, not surprising\"\n166\t          ],\n167\t          [\n168\t            \"Delta probe\",\n169\t            \"+0.011\",\n170\t            \"Same encoder → similar structure\"\n171\t          ],\n172\t          [\n173\t            \"Classification\",\n174\t            \"+0.001\",\n175\t            \"Trivially easy for both conditions\"\n176\t          ]\n177\t        ]\n178\t      }\n179\t    ],\n180\t    \"figures\": [],\n181\t    \"analysis\": \"6 methods consistency 从 \\\"strong evidence for trained ≈ untrained\\\" 降为\\n\\\"thorough but unsurprising verification of a structurally predicted outcome\\\"。\\nCKA reversal 使 \\\"all methods consistent\\\" claim 不成立。Framework reframe 下\\n唯一残余价值：demonstrate framework 的 multi-method coverage capability。\\n\\n\\nOrphaned 但子实验（RSA, R², CKA, action probe, delta probe, classification）均已完成。\\nWorst 档下 trained ≈ untrained 被视为 \\\"trivially expected under frozen encoder\\\"。\\nReviewer：\\\"frozen SigLIP+projector 输出相同 L0 features，LLM fine-tuning 只改变 weights\\n而非 input distribution——所以 intermediate layer representations naturally similar。\\n你用 6 种方法验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，这不是 thoroughness 而是 over-verification。\\\"\\nCKA ordering reversal 进一步削弱 multi-method consistency narrative——6 methods 中 CKA\\n反转了 RSA，说明 \\\"consistency\\\" 是 cherry-picked（只 consistent 在某些 metrics 下）。\\nWorst reviewer 总结：\\\"这些实验证明了 VLA > DINO 但 trained ≈ untrained——\\n前者 expected（LLM 有 4096d features vs DINO 1024d），后者 也 expected（same encoder）。\\\"\\n\"\n182\t  },\n183\t  {\n184\t    \"name\": \"Instruction ablation\",\n185\t    \"description\": \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\",\n186\t    \"results\": {\n187\t      \"delta_with_vs_no_inst\": 0.004,\n188\t      \"gate_judgment\": \"FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\"\n189\t    },\n190\t    \"tables\": [],\n191\t    \"figures\": [],\n192\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 下从 C3 evidence 降为 \\\"confirms structural prediction, not finding\\\"。\\nFramework reframe 下可作为 \\\"sanity check\\\" 一句带过，不占独立段落。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下被视为 tautological sanity check：image token RSA 在 causal mask 下\\n不受 instruction tokens 影响是 structural guarantee，不是 empirical finding。\\nReviewer：\\\"你在 C1 里承认 causal mask 使 image tokens 看不到 instructions，\\n然后在 plan_006 里'发现' image RSA 不受 instructions 影响——这是验证了你自己的前提假设。\\nΔ=0.004 是 noise，不是 small effect——effect 在结构上不可能存在。\\n这 0.5 页可以省掉或用一句话带过。\\\"\\n\"\n193\t  },\n194\t  {\n195\t    \"name\": \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\",\n196\t    \"description\": \"四条件全收敛验证\",\n197\t    \"results\": {\n198\t      \"trained_with_inst\": 0.488,\n199\t      \"trained_no_inst\": 0.489,\n200\t      \"untrained_with_inst\": 0.485,\n201\t      \"untrained_no_inst\": 0.48,\n202\t      \"bootstrap_ci_includes_0\": true,\n203\t      \"training_effect\": 0.003,\n204\t      \"instruction_effect\": 0.004\n205\t    },\n206\t    \"tables\": [\n207\t      {\n208\t        \"title\": \"2×2 Matrix as Expected Null (Worst-Tier)\",\n209\t        \"columns\": [\n210\t          \"Condition\",\n211\t          \"RSA\",\n212\t          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n213\t        ],\n214\t        \"rows\": [\n215\t          [\n216\t            \"Trained + Inst\",\n217\t            \"0.488\",\n218\t            \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"\n219\t          ],\n220\t          [\n221\t            \"Trained - Inst\",\n222\t            \"0.489\",\n223\t            \"Expected: causal mask blocks\"\n224\t          ],\n225\t          [\n226\t            \"Untrained + Inst\",\n227\t            \"0.485\",\n228\t            \"Expected: same encoder\"\n229\t          ],\n230\t          [\n231\t            \"Untrained - Inst\",\n232\t            \"0.480\",\n233\t            \"Expected: both factors null\"\n234\t          ]\n235\t        ]\n236\t      }\n237\t    ],\n238\t    \"figures\": [],\n239\t    \"analysis\": \"Framework reframe 下 2×2 matrix 的价值从 \\\"finding\\\" 转为 \\\"exemplar of factorial\\ndesign capability\\\"——可复用性贡献，但在 CoRL 不计高分。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下 2×2 null result 被视为 \\\"expected outcome of frozen encoder + causal mask\\\"。\\nReviewer：\\\"你的 2×2 factorial design 是好的 experimental methodology，但它发现了 predicted null——\\nboth factors (training, instruction) have no effect on image token RSA 因为 (1) encoder frozen,\\n(2) causal mask blocks instruction→image. 好的 experimental design + expected null result\\n= methodology paper contribution, not empirical contribution。如果这是 methodology paper\\n那 ok，但你 pitch 的是 empirical findings about VLA routing。\\\"\\n四条件收敛到 0.48-0.49 band 进一步证实 RSA 对 image tokens 是 ceiling+floor bounded by encoder quality。\\n\"\n240\t  },\n241\t  {\n242\t    \"name\": \"Random instruction control\",\n243\t    \"description\": \"随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\",\n244\t    \"results\": {\n245\t      \"normal_rsa\": 0.489,\n246\t      \"random_rsa\": 0.484,\n247\t      \"shuffled_rsa\": 0.483,\n248\t      \"empty_rsa\": 0.472,\n249\t      \"max_absolute_delta\": 0.017,\n250\t      \"instruction_invariant\": true\n251\t    },\n252\t    \"tables\": [],\n253\t    \"figures\": [],\n254\t    \"analysis\": \"006/007/008 三合一压缩为半段。Framework reframe 下仅作为 \\\"invariance verification\\\"\\nmethodology demo。在 worst tier 下浪费篇幅的风险 > 贡献。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。与 plan_006/007 同一逻辑链——causal mask 使 image token RSA 对 instruction content\\n天然不变。Worst reviewer：\\\"你用了三个 experiments（006/007/008）验证同一个 structurally guaranteed\\nnull result。Normal/random/shuffled/empty 全在 ±0.02 内不是 finding，是 noise around a\\nguaranteed null。这占了论文篇幅但不增加 contribution。在 8 页限制下，三个实验应压缩为 1 段 sanity check。\\\"\\n更刻薄的 reviewer：\\\"spending 3 experiments on 'image tokens don't see instruction tokens'\\nsuggests the authors don't fully understand their own architecture's causal mask structure.\\\"\\n\"\n255\t  },\n256\t  {\n257\t    \"name\": \"CKA verification\",\n258\t    \"description\": \"CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\",\n259\t    \"results\": {\n260\t      \"linear_cka_ordering\": \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO\",\n261\t      \"rsa_ordering\": \"projector > trained > untrained > DINO\",\n262\t      \"ordering_reversal\": true,\n263\t      \"last_preaction_cka\": 0.127\n264\t    },\n265\t    \"tables\": [\n266\t      {\n267\t        \"title\": \"Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst-Tier Authority Crisis)\",\n268\t        \"columns\": [\n269\t          \"Metric\",\n270\t          \"Ordering\",\n271\t          \"Implication\"\n272\t        ],\n273\t        \"rows\": [\n274\t          [\n275\t            \"RSA (geometric)\",\n276\t            \"SigLIP > T > U > DINO\",\n277\t            \"Training degrades geometry\"\n278\t          ],\n279\t          [\n280\t            \"CKA (global)\",\n281\t            \"U > T > SigLIP > DINO\",\n282\t            \"Training preserves/improves structure\"\n283\t          ],\n284\t          [\n285\t            \"R² (functional)\",\n286\t            \"T_lastpre > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img > U\",\n287\t            \"Training enables routing\"\n288\t          ],\n289\t          [\n290\t            \"Reviewer question\",\n291\t            \"—\",\n292\t            \"Framework credibility if metrics disagree?\"\n293\t          ]\n294\t        ]\n295\t      }\n296\t    ],\n297\t    \"figures\": [],\n298\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA dissociation 在 worst tier 下是 double-edged：可以包装为 \\\"why we need multi-metric\\nframework\\\" 但同时 undermines 所有 single-metric conclusions。Exit collapse 只在 R²\\n下明显——如果 CKA 下不 collapse，reviewer 要求 \\\"architecture-independent\\\" 必须\\n\\\"metric-independent\\\"，否则 claim 降级。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。CKA-RSA dissociation 在 worst 档下变得 doubly 致命。\\n第一层攻击（保持不变）：\\\"如果 CKA 说 untrained > trained 而 RSA 说 trained > untrained，\\n那哪个 metric 才反映 'action-relevant information'？你选了 RSA 来讲 story，但另一个\\nequally principled metric 给出相反结论。这不是 metric dissociation finding——\\n这是 your conclusions are metric-dependent 的 admission。\\\"\\n第二层攻击（D095 升级后更致命）：\\\"你们现在 claim R² exit collapse 是跨架构一致的\\nVLM→VLA signature。但 R² 本身是 functional metric（probe-based），RSA 是 geometric metric，\\nCKA 是 kernel-based metric。如果不同 metrics 给不同结论，你凭什么用 R² 的 exit collapse\\n而不是 CKA 的 no-collapse 来 claim 'architecture-independent signature'？\\n你的 framework 应该 reconcile 这些 metrics 而不是 pick 对你有利的那个。\\\"\\n\"\n299\t  },\n300\t  {\n301\t    \"name\": \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\",\n302\t    \"description\": \"第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\",\n303\t    \"results\": {\n304\t      \"trained_image_mean_peak_R2\": 0.696,\n305\t      \"trained_image_mean_peak_layer\": 13,\n306\t      \"trained_last_preaction_peak_R2\": 0.675,\n307\t      \"trained_last_preaction_peak_layer\": 21,\n308\t      \"untrained_image_mean_peak_R2\": 0.673,\n309\t      \"untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2\": 0.635,\n310\t      \"trained_vs_untrained_delta_imgmean\": 0.023,\n311\t      \"trained_vs_untrained_delta_lastpre\": 0.04,\n312\t      \"bootstrap_p\": 0.001\n313\t    },\n314\t    \"tables\": [\n315\t      {\n316\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Benchmark Comparison (OpenVLA Only)\",\n317\t        \"columns\": [\n318\t          \"Benchmark\",\n319\t          \"Delta (imgmean best-vs-best)\",\n320\t          \"Delta (lastpre best-vs-best)\",\n321\t          \"Worst Reading\"\n322\t        ],\n323\t        \"rows\": [\n324\t          [\n325\t            \"LIBERO-Goal\",\n326\t            \"0.015\",\n327\t            \"0.069\",\n328\t            \"Moderate; only architecture tested\"\n329\t          ],\n330\t          [\n331\t            \"LIBERO-Spatial\",\n332\t            \"0.023\",\n333\t            \"0.040\",\n334\t            \"Small; confirms VLA→VLA transition minimal\"\n335\t          ],\n336\t          [\n337\t            \"Implication\",\n338\t            \"—\",\n339\t            \"—\",\n340\t            \"Within-arch replication, not cross-arch validation\"\n341\t          ]\n342\t        ]\n343\t      }\n344\t    ],\n345\t    \"figures\": [],\n346\t    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark replication 有价值但不解决 cross-architecture gap。D102 framing 下\\nsmall delta 是 expected（VLA→VLA），但 reviewer 会用此攻击：\\\"如果进一步 finetuning\\n不 substantially change representations，studying finetuning effects 的意义何在？\\\"\\n\\n\\n数据已完成。Worst 档下此实验是 within-architecture cross-benchmark（仍是 OpenVLA），\\n不解决 RC4 的 cross-architecture concern。Reviewer：\\\"从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial\\n只是换了 task suite 不是换了 VLA 架构——这不回答 'does it generalize across architectures'。\\\"\\nSpatial 的 trained-untrained delta（best-vs-best）=0.023（imgmean）/ 0.040（lastpre）\\n小于 Goal 的 0.015/0.069。退一步看，R² exit collapse 在 D102 更新后被重新定义为\\nVLM→VLA transition effect——但 LIBERO-Spatial 和 Goal 都用同一个 OpenVLA checkpoint（已是 VLA），\\n所以 trained vs untrained（OXE vs LIBERO-finetuned）的 delta 本就该小（VLA→VLA transition）。\\n这与 D102 结论一致但在 worst tier 下被解读为 \\\"further fine-tuning doesn't change much\\n= fine-tuning doesn't matter much = your study of fine-tuning effects is studying something trivial。\\\"\\n\"\n347\t  },\n348\t  {\n349\t    \"name\": \"Full-layer R² scan\",\n350\t    \"description\": \"33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\",\n351\t    \"results\": {\n352\t      \"trained_image_mean_peak\": {\n353\t        \"layer\": 8,\n354\t        \"R2\": 0.655\n355\t      },\n356\t      \"trained_last_preaction_peak\": {\n357\t        \"layer\": 13,\n358\t        \"R2\": 0.678\n359\t      },\n360\t      \"untrained_image_mean_peak\": {\n361\t        \"layer\": 0,\n362\t        \"R2\": 0.64\n363\t      },\n364\t      \"untrained_last_preaction_peak\": {\n365\t        \"layer\": 32,\n366\t        \"R2\": 0.609\n367\t      },\n368\t      \"trained_exit_R2_lastpre\": 0.422,\n369\t      \"untrained_exit_R2_lastpre\": 0.545,\n370\t      \"exit_collapse_delta_lastpre\": 0.256,\n371\t      \"best_vs_best_lastpre_delta\": 0.069,\n372\t      \"best_vs_best_lastpre_p\": 0.0001\n373\t    },\n374\t    \"tables\": [\n375\t      {\n376\t        \"title\": \"R² Exit Collapse with D100/D102 Context (Worst-Tier)\",\n377\t        \"columns\": [\n378\t          \"Condition\",\n379\t          \"Peak R²\",\n380\t          \"Exit R²\",\n381\t          \"Δ\",\n382\t          \"Worst Interpretation\"\n383\t        ],\n384\t        \"rows\": [\n385\t          [\n386\t            \"VLA trained\",\n387\t            \"0.678 (L13)\",\n388\t            \"0.422 (L32)\",\n389\t            \"0.256\",\n390\t            \"Action head 'consumes' info — trivially expected\"\n391\t          ],\n392\t          [\n393\t            \"OXE untrained\",\n394\t            \"0.609 (L32)\",\n395\t            \"0.609 (L32)\",\n396\t            \"0.000\",\n397\t            \"No exit collapse — consistent with VLA→VLA null\"\n398\t          ],\n399\t          [\n400\t            \"Llama-2-chat (D100)\",\n401\t            \"0.156 (all)\",\n402\t            \"0.156 (all)\",\n403\t            \"0.000\",\n404\t            \"NLP: flat noise floor, no action info anywhere\"\n405\t          ],\n406\t          [\n407\t            \"Random init\",\n408\t            \"0.640 (L0)\",\n409\t            \"~0 (L10-L13)\",\n410\t            \"pathological\",\n411\t            \"Not valid control — random weights meaningless\"\n412\t          ]\n413\t        ]\n414\t      }\n415\t    ],\n416\t    \"figures\": [],\n417\t    \"analysis\": \"D100 NLP control 排除了 generic fine-tuning confound，这是论文的防御性胜利。但 worst reviewer\\n的 next-level 攻击——exit collapse 是 \\\"action consumption\\\" 而非 \\\"routing mechanism\\\"——\\n仍然 stands without behavioral validation。Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个区分\\n并 position exit collapse 为 \\\"diagnostic indicator of action training stage\\\" 而非 \\\"mechanistic finding\\\"。\\n\\n\\n数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头实验。D100 NLP control 已排除\\ngeneric fine-tuning confound（Llama-2-chat ΔR²=0.000），D102 将其定义为 VLM→VLA transition effect。\\n但 worst-tier reviewer 反转 D100/D102：\\n\\\"D100 证明 NLP finetuning 不产生 exit collapse——好。但这只说明 exit collapse 需要 action training，\\n不说明它有 functional significance。VLM→VLA transition 当然改变 exit layer——action head 需要从\\nexit layer decode 7-DOF actions，这不是 routing 'discovery' 而是 'the model learned to produce actions\\nand the last layer reflects that'。你的 R² probe 测量的是 Ridge regression 从 hidden states 预测 actions\\n的能力——exit layer R² 下降只是说明 action-relevant information 被 'consumed' by action decoding，\\n不是被 'discarded' by routing mechanism。这是 trivially expected under any encoder-decoder framework。\\\"\\nWorst reviewer 要求 behavioral evidence：如果 exit collapse 是 functional routing，\\nablating exit-layer representations 应该 disproportionately affect task performance——但这从未被测试。\\n\"\n418\t  },\n419\t  {\n420\t    \"name\": \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\",\n421\t    \"description\": \"CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\",\n422\t    \"results\": {\n423\t      \"clip_rsa\": 0.557,\n424\t      \"clip_R2\": 0.587,\n425\t      \"dino_cls_rsa\": 0.692,\n426\t      \"dino_cls_R2\": 0.634,\n427\t      \"projector_R2\": 0.63,\n428\t      \"vl_pretraining_not_superior\": true\n429\t    },\n430\t    \"tables\": [\n431\t      {\n432\t        \"title\": \"Encoder Quality vs Language Supervision\",\n433\t        \"columns\": [\n434\t          \"Encoder\",\n435\t          \"RSA\",\n436\t          \"R²\",\n437\t          \"Has Language?\",\n438\t          \"Worst Implication\"\n439\t        ],\n440\t        \"rows\": [\n441\t          [\n442\t            \"DINO cls\",\n443\t            \"0.692\",\n444\t            \"0.634\",\n445\t            \"No\",\n446\t            \"Best in both — language supervision unnecessary\"\n447\t          ],\n448\t          [\n449\t            \"SigLIP+Proj\",\n450\t            \"0.615\",\n451\t            \"0.630\",\n452\t            \"Yes\",\n453\t            \"VL pretraining inferior to DINO\"\n454\t          ],\n455\t          [\n456\t            \"CLIP ViT-L\",\n457\t            \"0.557\",\n458\t            \"0.587\",\n459\t            \"Yes\",\n460\t            \"Worst VL encoder\"\n461\t          ],\n462\t          [\n463\t            \"Implication\",\n464\t            \"—\",\n465\t            \"—\",\n466\t            \"—\",\n467\t            \"Language supervision may hurt encoder quality\"\n468\t          ]\n469\t        ]\n470\t      }\n471\t    ],\n472\t    \"figures\": [],\n473\t    \"analysis\": \"CLIP control 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining superiority，更挑战整篇论文的\\nmotivation。Framework reframe 可以 spin 为 \\\"framework reveals that language supervision\\nand action quality are decoupled\\\" 但这是 defensive 而非 proactive contribution。\\n\\n\\n数据已完成：CLIP < DINO in both RSA and R²。VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。\\nWorst 档延伸攻击：\\\"CLIP < DINO 说明 language-supervised pretraining 不帮助 action representation。\\n那为什么 VLA 要用 language-supervised encoder（SigLIP）而非 self-supervised（DINO）？更关键的是：\\n如果最好的 action-relevant encoder 不需要 language，你们花整篇论文研究 instruction routing\\n的 practical relevance 在哪里？Instructions 在 VLA 中可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\\n你们应该研究为什么 VLA 不用 DINO 作为 encoder，而非研究 instruction 如何 route through LLM。\\\"\\n这直接挑战论文 premise 而非 findings——worst tier 下论文可能被判 \\\"interesting but\\nfundamentally misdirected\\\"。\\n\"\n474\t  },\n475\t  {\n476\t    \"name\": \"Branch-split RSA\",\n477\t    \"description\": \"DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\",\n478\t    \"results\": {\n479\t      \"dinov2_branch_rsa\": 0.619,\n480\t      \"siglip_branch_rsa\": 0.621,\n481\t      \"fused_rsa\": 0.634,\n482\t      \"post_projector_rsa\": 0.615\n483\t    },\n484\t    \"tables\": [],\n485\t    \"figures\": [],\n486\t    \"analysis\": \"Architecture-specific detail，appendix material。Framework demo 价值存在但不值得 main text 篇幅。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP in fused backbone（Δ<0.002）。Worst 档下此实验只适用于\\nOpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP 架构。TracVLA 和 NORA 用完全不同的 vision encoders，\\nbranch-split 不可迁移。Reviewer：\\\"这是 architecture-specific implementation detail，\\n不是 generalizable finding。在 8-page 限制下应移到 appendix。\\\"\\n在 diagnostic framework reframe 下可保留为 \\\"framework 能做 sub-encoder analysis\\\" demo，\\n但 0.5 段就够了。\\n\"\n487\t  },\n488\t  {\n489\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix (D096/D099/D102)\",\n490\t    \"description\": \"3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse — D102 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离\",\n491\t    \"results\": {\n492\t      \"total_cells\": 10,\n493\t      \"vlm_to_vla_cells\": 6,\n494\t      \"vlm_to_vla_all_substantial\": true,\n495\t      \"vlm_to_vla_delta_range\": [\n496\t        0.156,\n497\t        0.455\n498\t      ],\n499\t      \"vla_to_vla_cells\": 4,\n500\t      \"vla_to_vla_none_substantial\": true,\n501\t      \"vla_to_vla_delta_range\": [\n502\t        0.033,\n503\t        0.086\n504\t      ],\n505\t      \"nlp_control_delta\": 0.0,\n506\t      \"binary_separation\": \"VLM→VLA 6/6 vs VLA→VLA 0/4\",\n507\t      \"tracvla_goal_delta\": 0.228,\n508\t      \"tracvla_spatial_delta\": 0.138,\n509\t      \"tracvla_object_delta\": 0.294,\n510\t      \"tracvla_long_delta\": 0.198,\n511\t      \"nora_goal_delta\": 0.691,\n512\t      \"nora_spatial_delta\": 0.302,\n513\t      \"openvla_goal_delta\": 0.086,\n514\t      \"openvla_spatial_delta\": 0.037,\n515\t      \"openvla_object_delta\": 0.037,\n516\t      \"openvla_long_delta\": 0.033\n517\t    },\n518\t    \"tables\": [\n519\t      {\n520\t        \"title\": \"R² Exit Collapse: D102 Binary Separation (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\",\n521\t        \"columns\": [\n522\t          \"Transition Type\",\n523\t          \"Architecture\",\n524\t          \"Suite\",\n525\t          \"Δ (peak-exit)\",\n526\t          \"Worst Reading\"\n527\t        ],\n528\t        \"rows\": [\n529\t          [\n530\t            \"VLM→VLA\",\n531\t            \"TracVLA (Phi-3→VLA)\",\n532\t            \"Goal\",\n533\t            \"0.228\",\n534\t            \"Expected: domain adaptation reorganization\"\n535\t          ],\n536\t          [\n537\t            \"VLM→VLA\",\n538\t            \"TracVLA\",\n539\t            \"Spatial\",\n540\t            \"0.138\",\n541\t            \"Expected: same mechanism\"\n542\t          ],\n543\t          [\n544\t            \"VLM→VLA\",\n545\t            \"TracVLA\",\n546\t            \"Object\",\n547\t            \"0.294\",\n548\t            \"Expected: same mechanism\"\n549\t          ],\n550\t          [\n551\t            \"VLM→VLA\",\n552\t            \"TracVLA\",\n553\t            \"Long\",\n554\t            \"0.198\",\n555\t            \"Expected: same mechanism\"\n556\t          ],\n557\t          [\n558\t            \"VLM→VLA\",\n559\t            \"NORA (Qwen2.5→VLA)\",\n560\t            \"Goal\",\n561\t            \"0.691\",\n562\t            \"Outlier: 3x median, architecture-specific\"\n563\t          ],\n564\t          [\n565\t            \"VLM→VLA\",\n566\t            \"NORA\",\n567\t            \"Spatial\",\n568\t            \"0.302\",\n569\t            \"Expected: consistent with NORA pattern\"\n570\t          ],\n571\t          [\n572\t            \"VLA→VLA\",\n573\t            \"OpenVLA (OXE→LIBERO)\",\n574\t            \"Goal\",\n575\t            \"0.086\",\n576\t            \"Below threshold: no new collapse\"\n577\t          ],\n578\t          [\n579\t            \"VLA→VLA\",\n580\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n581\t            \"Spatial\",\n582\t            \"0.037\",\n583\t            \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"\n584\t          ],\n585\t          [\n586\t            \"VLA→VLA\",\n587\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n588\t            \"Object\",\n589\t            \"0.037\",\n590\t            \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"\n591\t          ],\n592\t          [\n593\t            \"VLA→VLA\",\n594\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n595\t            \"Long\",\n596\t            \"0.033\",\n597\t            \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"\n598\t          ]\n599\t        ]\n600\t      },\n601\t      {\n602\t        \"title\": \"Exit Collapse Diagnostic Value Assessment\",\n603\t        \"columns\": [\n604\t          \"Question\",\n605\t          \"Answer\",\n606\t          \"Practical Value\"\n607\t        ],\n608\t        \"rows\": [\n609\t          [\n610\t            \"Does model show VLM→VLA transition?\",\n611\t            \"Yes, 6/6 cells\",\n612\t            \"Low: practitioner already knows training history\"\n613\t          ],\n614\t          [\n615\t            \"Can it track ongoing optimization?\",\n616\t            \"No, 0/4 VLA→VLA cells\",\n617\t            \"Zero: one-time marker only\"\n618\t          ],\n619\t          [\n620\t            \"Is magnitude calibrated?\",\n621\t            \"No, 4.4x range within VLM→VLA\",\n622\t            \"Low: cannot compare across architectures\"\n623\t          ],\n624\t          [\n625\t            \"Does NLP control exclude confound?\",\n626\t            \"Yes, D100 ΔR²=0.000\",\n627\t            \"Defensive win but doesn't add value\"\n628\t          ]\n629\t        ]\n630\t      }\n631\t    ],\n632\t    \"figures\": [],\n633\t    \"analysis\": \"D102 binary separation 是 scientifically clean 但 worst-tier reviewer 把 clean result\\n重新定义为 trivial result。NLP control 是 necessary defense 但不 sufficient to elevate\\ncontribution。Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \\\"one-time transition marker detected\\nby framework\\\" 而非 \\\"architecture-independent routing signature\\\"。价值在 framework 能\\nsystematically detect transition effects 而非 the specific effect detected。\\n\\n\\nD102 更新后数据清晰：VLM→VLA transition 6/6 一致（Δ=0.156-0.455），VLA→VLA 0/4 超过 Δ>0.10\\n阈值（Δ=0.033-0.086）。v3 MCCV 修正了 train-test leakage。D100 NLP control ΔR²=0.000\\n排除了 generic fine-tuning confound。\\n\\n但 worst-tier reviewer 用 D102 的 clean binary 反过来攻击：\\n\\\"你们自己证明了 exit collapse 是 one-time VLM→VLA transition artifact。这很好，但：\\n(1) 这不是 mechanism discovery——当你把 language model 变成 action model，出口层表征\\n当然会重组。任何 domain adaptation（NLP→vision, text→audio）都可能产生类似 transition effects。\\n你排除了 NLP finetuning，但没排除其他 domain adaptation scenarios（e.g., LLM→code generation）。\\n(2) 作为 diagnostic tool 的价值有限：exit collapse 只告诉你 'this model was once a VLM\\nthat got converted to VLA'——但在实践中你已经知道这一点（你知道模型的 training pipeline）。\\n什么时候 practitioner 需要一个 tool 来判断 '我的模型是不是 VLA'？\\n(3) VLA→VLA finetuning 无 exit collapse（0/4）说明它不是 ongoing routing optimization 的\\nindicator——它只是 initial adaptation 的 one-time marker。一个只出现一次的 diagnostic \\n不能用于 iterative VLA development。\\n(4) Magnitude 仍然高度 variable（0.156-0.691, 4.4x range even within VLM→VLA cells），\\nNORA 的 0.691 是 outlier（3x median）。Architecture-independent 的 direction 但\\narchitecture-dependent 的 magnitude——这降低了作为 quantitative diagnostic 的 precision。\\\"\\n\\nD100 NLP control 是 good defense 但不足以救 worst tier——因为 reviewer 的攻击不是\\n\\\"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning\\\" 而是 \\\"exit collapse is trivially expected VLM→VLA transition\\\"。\\n\"\n634\t  },\n635\t  {\n636\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Base-Model vs Training)\",\n637\t    \"description\": \"3 架构 L1 instruction-dominant heads — D090 证明 base-model-dependent\",\n638\t    \"results\": {\n639\t      \"openvla_trained\": 23,\n640\t      \"openvla_oxe_untrained\": 26,\n641\t      \"tracvla_trained\": [\n642\t        27,\n643\t        30\n644\t      ],\n645\t      \"tracvla_untrained_vlm\": 32,\n646\t      \"nora_trained\": [\n647\t        12,\n648\t        13\n649\t      ],\n650\t      \"nora_untrained_vlm\": [\n651\t        13,\n652\t        14\n653\t      ],\n654\t      \"training_effect_on_l1\": \"none or negative\"\n655\t    },\n656\t    \"tables\": [\n657\t      {\n658\t        \"title\": \"L1 Heads: Training Contributes Nothing (D090 Worst Reading)\",\n659\t        \"columns\": [\n660\t          \"Architecture\",\n661\t          \"Base Model\",\n662\t          \"Trained\",\n663\t          \"Untrained\",\n664\t          \"Training Δ\"\n665\t        ],\n666\t        \"rows\": [\n667\t          [\n668\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n669\t            \"Llama-2-7B\",\n670\t            \"24/32\",\n671\t            \"0/32 (random init)\",\n672\t            \"Artifact: random has no LM\"\n673\t          ],\n674\t          [\n675\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n676\t            \"OXE-pretrained\",\n677\t            \"24/32\",\n678\t            \"25/32 (OXE)\",\n679\t            \"-1: OXE already saturated\"\n680\t          ],\n681\t          [\n682\t            \"TracVLA\",\n683\t            \"Phi-3-mini\",\n684\t            \"27-30/32\",\n685\t            \"32/32 (VLM base)\",\n686\t            \"-2 to -5: training REDUCES\"\n687\t          ],\n688\t          [\n689\t            \"NORA\",\n690\t            \"Qwen2.5-VL-3B\",\n691\t            \"12-13/16\",\n692\t            \"13-14/16\",\n693\t            \"-1: no training effect\"\n694\t          ]\n695\t        ]\n696\t      },\n697\t      {\n698\t        \"title\": \"Contribution Audit After D090\",\n699\t        \"columns\": [\n700\t          \"Originally Claimed\",\n701\t          \"Post-D090 Status\",\n702\t          \"Remaining Value\"\n703\t        ],\n704\t        \"rows\": [\n705\t          [\n706\t            \"L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\",\n707\t            \"REMOVED: base-model artifact\",\n708\t            \"Zero\"\n709\t          ],\n710\t          [\n711\t            \"Bookend attention pattern\",\n712\t            \"WEAKENED: entry from base model\",\n713\t            \"Exit engagement only\"\n714\t          ],\n715\t          [\n716\t            \"R² exit collapse\",\n717\t            \"Retained: training-induced\",\n718\t            \"Thin — one-time transition\"\n719\t          ],\n720\t          [\n721\t            \"CF sensitivity\",\n722\t            \"Retained: training-induced\",\n723\t            \"Thin — unfair baselines\"\n724\t          ],\n725\t          [\n726\t            \"Experimental framework\",\n727\t            \"Intact\",\n728\t            \"Main surviving contribution\"\n729\t          ]\n730\t        ]\n731\t      }\n732\t    ],\n733\t    \"figures\": [],\n734\t    \"analysis\": \"D090 是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe 试图把 D090 从 weakness 转为\\n\\\"framework's key capability: distinguishing training-induced from pre-existing\\\"——\\n但 reviewer 可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。核心问题：能区分 training vs pretraining\\neffects 是 methodology 贡献，但 CoRL 评审 findings 而非 methods。\\n\\n\\nD090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent。Worst tier 核心攻击：\\n\\\"L1 routing gradient（0→9→24 heads）是论文最 visually striking 的结果，但你们自己证明了\\n它不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained（纯 VLM）已 32/32，训练反而减少到 27-30（repurposing）。\\nNORA untrained 已 13-14/16，训练无变化。OpenVLA 的 0→24 gradient 只是 random init vs\\npretrained 的差异——任何 pretrained LLM 都有 instruction attention heads，不需要 VLA training。\\n\\n这意味着论文最核心的 visual result（Figure X 的 attention head gradient）不能 claim\\n是 VLA training 的贡献。读者看到这个图会以为训练创造了 routing——但实际上 routing 来自\\nlanguage pretraining。这是 misleading framing，即使你在正文中有 caveat。\\\"\\n\\nD090 后 remaining training-induced effects 只剩 exit collapse 和 CF sensitivity。\\nReviewer 总结：\\\"After D090, VLA training's unique contribution is one transition artifact\\n(exit collapse) and one baseline-confounded sensitivity measure (CF). This is too thin\\nfor a full paper at a top robotics venue.\\\"\\n\"\n735\t  },\n736\t  {\n737\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\",\n738\t    \"description\": \"3 架构 CF sensitivity — trained vs untrained 对比\",\n739\t    \"results\": {\n740\t      \"openvla_goal_trained_d\": 1.182,\n741\t      \"openvla_goal_untrained_d\": 1.048,\n742\t      \"openvla_spatial_trained_d\": 1.173,\n743\t      \"openvla_spatial_untrained_d\": 0.936,\n744\t      \"tracvla_goal_trained_d\": 1.524,\n745\t      \"tracvla_goal_untrained_cos\": 0.153,\n746\t      \"nora_goal_trained_cos\": 1.0,\n747\t      \"nora_goal_untrained_cos\": 0.081,\n748\t      \"incommensurable_pairs\": 5,\n749\t      \"fair_comparison_pairs\": 2,\n750\t      \"openvla_goal_fair_delta\": 0.134,\n751\t      \"openvla_spatial_fair_delta\": 0.237\n752\t    },\n753\t    \"tables\": [\n754\t      {\n755\t        \"title\": \"CF Sensitivity: Incommensurability Problem\",\n756\t        \"columns\": [\n757\t          \"Architecture\",\n758\t          \"Suite\",\n759\t          \"Trained Metric\",\n760\t          \"Untrained Metric\",\n761\t          \"Comparable?\",\n762\t          \"Fair Δ\"\n763\t        ],\n764\t        \"rows\": [\n765\t          [\n766\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n767\t            \"Goal\",\n768\t            \"d=1.182\",\n769\t            \"d=1.048\",\n770\t            \"Yes\",\n771\t            \"+0.134 (12%)\"\n772\t          ],\n773\t          [\n774\t            \"OpenVLA\",\n775\t            \"Spatial\",\n776\t            \"d=1.173\",\n777\t            \"d=0.936\",\n778\t            \"Yes\",\n779\t            \"+0.237 (25%)\"\n780\t          ],\n781\t          [\n782\t            \"TracVLA\",\n783\t            \"Goal\",\n784\t            \"d=1.524\",\n785\t            \"cos=0.153\",\n786\t            \"No\",\n787\t            \"Incommensurable\"\n788\t          ],\n789\t          [\n790\t            \"TracVLA\",\n791\t            \"Spatial\",\n792\t            \"d=1.333\",\n793\t            \"cos=0.180\",\n794\t            \"No\",\n795\t            \"Incommensurable\"\n796\t          ],\n797\t          [\n798\t            \"TracVLA\",\n799\t            \"Object\",\n800\t            \"d=1.212\",\n801\t            \"cos=0.185\",\n802\t            \"No\",\n803\t            \"Incommensurable\"\n804\t          ],\n805\t          [\n806\t            \"TracVLA\",\n807\t            \"Long\",\n808\t            \"d=1.473\",\n809\t            \"cos=0.173\",\n810\t            \"No\",\n811\t            \"Incommensurable\"\n812\t          ],\n813\t          [\n814\t            \"NORA\",\n815\t            \"Goal\",\n816\t            \"cos=1.0 (sat.)\",\n817\t            \"cos=0.081\",\n818\t            \"Partially\",\n819\t            \"Saturated — ceiling artifact?\"\n820\t          ]\n821\t        ]\n822\t      },\n823\t      {\n824\t        \"title\": \"CF Sensitivity: Missing Behavioral Validation\",\n825\t        \"columns\": [\n826\t          \"What CF Shows\",\n827\t          \"What Reviewer Wants\",\n828\t          \"Gap\"\n829\t        ],\n830\t        \"rows\": [\n831\t          [\n832\t            \"Output direction changes (d>0.5)\",\n833\t            \"Task success rate drops\",\n834\t            \"No closed-loop data\"\n835\t          ],\n836\t          [\n837\t            \"Empty > wrong > shuffled > para\",\n838\t            \"Perturbation severity → failure rate correlation\",\n839\t            \"No behavioral grounding\"\n840\t          ],\n841\t          [\n842\t            \"ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth\",\n843\t            \"Action quality under perturbation\",\n844\t            \"MSE≈0 suggests no quality impact\"\n845\t          ]\n846\t        ]\n847\t      }\n848\t    ],\n849\t    \"figures\": [],\n850\t    \"analysis\": \"CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下被 double-attacked: incommensurable metrics + no behavioral\\ngrounding。ΔMSE≈0 (ground-truth error unchanged under ablation) is particularly damaging——\\nit suggests CF perturbation changes output direction without degrading quality，\\nsupporting \\\"information-computation dissociation\\\" (Hewitt & Liang 2019) interpretation\\nthat routing modulates output but doesn't encode task-critical information。\\nFramework reframe：CF analysis 降为 \\\"framework's perturbation analysis capability\\\"，\\nbehavioral validation 列为 \\\"critical future work\\\"。\\n\\n\\nD097/D099 修正后，CF sensitivity 的 cross-architecture 对比面临 incommensurability 问题：\\nTracVLA/NORA untrained 无法生成 actions（cosine in hidden space），trained 用 Cohen's d\\nin action space——两个 metrics 不可直接比较。只有 OpenVLA 的 trained + untrained 都能生成\\nactions，可用同一 metric 比较。\\n\\nWorst-tier reviewer 攻击：\\n\\\"CF sensitivity 是你们仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后），但：\\n(1) 你们自己承认 5/7 cross-architecture comparisons 使用 incommensurable metrics（Cohen's d\\nvs cosine distance）。你不能 claim 'training amplifies CF sensitivity' 如果 trained 和\\nuntrained 用不同 metrics 测量——这不是 methodological nuance，这是 fundamental flaw。\\n(2) 唯一公平对比（OpenVLA Goal/Spatial）显示 Δ=+0.13/+0.24，即 trained 比 untrained\\n高 12%/25%。但 OpenVLA untrained 是 OXE-pretrained VLA（已有 strong CF d=1.048），\\n所以 'training amplification' 是 VLA→VLA marginal improvement 而非 VLM→VLA dramatic change。\\n(3) 'Empty instruction produces largest deviation' 在 6/8 settings——这不需要 VLA-specific\\nrouting 来解释。任何 conditioned generative model 在 input 被完全移除时 output 会 change most。\\n这是 conditioning 的 definition 而非 routing mechanism。\\n(4) CF sensitivity 没有 behavioral grounding：output changes（d=0.65-1.5）是否\\n导致 task failure？如果 perturbed instructions 产生 different but equally valid actions，\\nCF sensitivity 不是 routing evidence 而是 representational noise。\\n缺少 behavioral validation（closed-loop success rate under perturbation）是 near-fatal\\nfor CoRL submission。\\\"\\n\"\n851\t  },\n852\t  {\n853\t    \"name\": \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\",\n854\t    \"description\": \"VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\",\n855\t    \"results\": {\n856\t      \"tier1_models\": [\n857\t        \"Phi-3-Vision\",\n858\t        \"Qwen2.5-VL\",\n859\t        \"random init Llama-2\"\n860\t      ],\n861\t      \"tier1_l1_heads\": [\n862\t        32,\n863\t        14,\n864\t        0\n865\t      ],\n866\t      \"tier1_cf_max_cos\": 0.19,\n867\t      \"tier1_exit_collapse\": false,\n868\t      \"tier2_model\": \"openvla-7b (OXE)\",\n869\t      \"tier2_l1_heads\": 25,\n870\t      \"tier2_cf_d\": 1.048,\n871\t      \"tier2_exit_collapse\": false,\n872\t      \"tier3_l1_heads\": [\n873\t        24,\n874\t        30,\n875\t        13\n876\t      ],\n877\t      \"tier3_exit_collapse_vlm_origin\": true,\n878\t      \"tier3_exit_collapse_vla_origin\": false,\n879\t      \"tier2_n_datapoints\": 1\n880\t    },\n881\t    \"tables\": [\n882\t      {\n883\t        \"title\": \"Three-Tier Gradient: N=1 at Tier-2\",\n884\t        \"columns\": [\n885\t          \"Tier\",\n886\t          \"N Models\",\n887\t          \"Key Metrics\",\n888\t          \"Worst Reading\"\n889\t        ],\n890\t        \"rows\": [\n891\t          [\n892\t            \"Tier 1 (VLM)\",\n893\t            \"3+\",\n894\t            \"L1: 0-32; CF<0.2; no collapse\",\n895\t            \"Adequate N but heterogeneous (0 vs 32 heads)\"\n896\t          ],\n897\t          [\n898\t            \"Tier 2 (General VLA)\",\n899\t            \"1 ONLY\",\n900\t            \"L1: 25; CF d=1.05; no collapse\",\n901\t            \"N=1 — cannot establish gradient\"\n902\t          ],\n903\t          [\n904\t            \"Tier 3 (Task VLA)\",\n905\t            \"~10 cells\",\n906\t            \"L1: 13-30; CF d>0.45; collapse if VLM-origin\",\n907\t            \"Adequate N but split by origin\"\n908\t          ]\n909\t        ]\n910\t      }\n911\t    ],\n912\t    \"figures\": [],\n913\t    \"analysis\": \"Three-tier gradient 必须移除或降为 \\\"preliminary observation with N=1 at intermediate tier\\\"。\\nFramework reframe：不 claim gradient，改为 \\\"framework enables stage-wise comparison\\\"——\\ncontribute methodology for comparing training stages, not the gradient finding itself.\\n\\n\\n三层级梯度被 worst reviewer 驳为 post-hoc narrative with N=1 at Tier-2。\\n\\n攻击 1 — 统计力不足：\\\"Tier-2 只有一个数据点（openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。要建立 gradient\\n你需要 at minimum 3 个独立的 OXE-pretrained 或 general-pretrained VLA checkpoints 来\\n验证 Tier-2 不是 openvla-7b specific。Three points don't make a gradient if the middle\\none is N=1——那是 step function with one interpolation point。\\\"\\n\\n攻击 2 — L1 heads 在 tiers 间不单调：\\\"Tier-1 Phi-3-Vision = 32/32, Tier-2 OXE = 25/32,\\nTier-3 TracVLA = 27-30/32。Tier-1 > Tier-2 ≈ Tier-3——这不是 gradient，这是 'base model\\nalready saturated then training reduces some heads'。L1 head count 不支持 gradient narrative。\\\"\\n\\n攻击 3 — Exit collapse 不支持 gradient：\\\"Tier-2 无 exit collapse, Tier-3 有 exit collapse\\n只在 VLM→VLA origin models——这是 binary transition 不是 gradient。如果 Tier-3 只在\\nVLM-origin 有 collapse 而 VLA-origin 没有，那 'gradient' 应该有 collapse 强度在 Tier-2→Tier-3\\nincreasing——但 Tier-2 = 0, Tier-3 (VLA origin) = 0。只有 Tier-3 (VLM origin) 有 collapse。\\n这是 binary (VLM→VLA collapse exists / doesn't) 不是 three-tier gradient。\\\"\\n\\n攻击 4 — libero_finetuned attention data 反驳 gradient：\\\"L31 exit engagement 从 bridge-VLA\\n(18 heads) 到 libero-finetuned (0 heads)——further specialization REDUCES exit routing。\\nGradient predicts 'more training = more routing' 但 data shows opposite at exit layer。\\\"\\n\"\n914\t  },\n915\t  {\n916\t    \"name\": \"NLP Finetuning Control (D100)\",\n917\t    \"description\": \"Llama-2-7b-chat R² profile 排除 generic fine-tuning confound\",\n918\t    \"results\": {\n919\t      \"peak_r2\": 0.1555,\n920\t      \"exit_r2\": 0.1555,\n921\t      \"delta_r2\": 0.0,\n922\t      \"profile_shape\": \"flat constant across all 32 layers\",\n923\t      \"r2_range\": [\n924\t        0.1547,\n925\t        0.1555\n926\t      ],\n927\t      \"phi3_nlp_delta\": 0.0,\n928\t      \"qwen_nlp_delta\": 0.0\n929\t    },\n930\t    \"tables\": [\n931\t      {\n932\t        \"title\": \"NLP Finetuning Control Results\",\n933\t        \"columns\": [\n934\t          \"Model\",\n935\t          \"Backbone\",\n936\t          \"ΔR²\",\n937\t          \"Profile\",\n938\t          \"Worst Reading\"\n939\t        ],\n940\t        \"rows\": [\n941\t          [\n942\t            \"Llama-2-7b-chat\",\n943\t            \"Llama-2-7B\",\n944\t            \"0.000\",\n945\t            \"Flat 0.155\",\n946\t            \"Expected: no action info anywhere\"\n947\t          ],\n948\t          [\n949\t            \"Phi-3-mini-instruct\",\n950\t            \"Phi-3-mini\",\n951\t            \"0.000\",\n952\t            \"Flat 0.155\",\n953\t            \"Expected: same noise floor\"\n954\t          ],\n955\t          [\n956\t            \"Qwen2.5-3B-instruct\",\n957\t            \"Qwen2.5-3B\",\n958\t            \"0.000\",\n959\t            \"Flat 0.155\",\n960\t            \"Expected: same noise floor\"\n961\t          ],\n962\t          [\n963\t            \"VLM→VLA (TracVLA)\",\n964\t            \"Phi-3-mini\",\n965\t            \"0.156-0.294\",\n966\t            \"Exit collapse\",\n967\t            \"VLA-specific but trivially expected\"\n968\t          ],\n969\t          [\n970\t            \"VLA→VLA (OpenVLA)\",\n971\t            \"Llama-2-7B\",\n972\t            \"0.033-0.086\",\n973\t            \"Mild decline\",\n974\t            \"No new collapse in VLA→VLA\"\n975\t          ]\n976\t        ]\n977\t      }\n978\t    ],\n979\t    \"figures\": [],\n980\t    \"analysis\": \"D100 是 necessary but not sufficient defense。Worst reviewer accepts the control\\nbut doesn't give credit for it — \\\"excluding an obvious confound is minimum bar,\\nnot contribution.\\\" Framework reframe 可以 cite D100 作为 \\\"framework enables\\ncross-domain comparison\\\" demo，但 reviewer 的 next-level attack（trivially expected）\\n仍 stands。\\n\\n\\nD100 结果 clean：三个 NLP-finetuned LLM（Llama-2-chat, Phi-3-instruct, Qwen2.5-instruct）\\n均 ΔR²=0.000，flat R²≈0.155 noise floor。这排除了 \\\"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning artifact\\\"。\\n\\n但 worst-tier reviewer 不被 impressed：\\n\\\"D100 是 good negative control，我们接受 exit collapse 不是 generic fine-tuning。\\n但这不能 elevate exit collapse 为 interesting finding——它只从 'might be generic artifact'\\n升级为 'VLA-specific but trivially expected'。当你训练一个 language model 来 predict\\n7-DOF robot actions，exit layer 表征当然会被 action training reshape。\\nR²≈0.155 in NLP models 只是说明 NLP models 没有 action-relevant information 在任何层\\n（Ridge 只拟合 between-task variance）——当然不会有 exit collapse。\\n你排除了一个 straw-man confound 但没有建立 positive value。\\nA good control experiment answers 'is this finding real?' — yours answers 'is this finding\\neven more trivially explainable than I thought?'  答案是 No，但 the finding is still trivial。\\\"\\n\\nR²=0.155 本身是 between-task variance baseline（10 tasks → Ridge 可拟合 task identity → \\n0.155 R² from 10-way between-task variance alone）——这是 expected 而非 surprising。\\n\"\n981\t  },\n982\t  {\n983\t    \"name\": \"Cross-Instruction Classification (C1 Framework)\",\n984\t    \"description\": \"10-way instruction classification 跨层 × 跨条件 — C1 框架核心实验\",\n985\t    \"results\": {\n986\t      \"trained_L1_acc\": 0.996,\n987\t      \"trained_L2_to_L31\": 1.0,\n988\t      \"llama2base_L1_acc\": 0.802,\n989\t      \"llama2base_L5_plus\": 1.0,\n990\t      \"untrained_L1_acc\": 1.0,\n991\t      \"untrained_L31_acc\": 0.82,\n992\t      \"image_mean_all_layers\": 0.1,\n993\t      \"loocv_trained\": \"100.00±0.00\",\n994\t      \"loocv_untrained\": \"84.76±11.59\"\n995\t    },\n996\t    \"tables\": [\n997\t      {\n998\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Instruction Classification: Trivially Easy?\",\n999\t        \"columns\": [\n1000\t          \"Condition\",\n1001\t          \"L1 Acc\",\n1002\t          \"L31 Acc\",\n1003\t          \"Worst Reading\"\n1004\t        ],\n1005\t        \"rows\": [\n1006\t          [\n1007\t            \"Trained\",\n1008\t            \"99.6%\",\n1009\t            \"100%\",\n1010\t            \"Flat 100% = ceiling effect, no gradient to analyze\"\n1011\t          ],\n1012\t          [\n1013\t            \"Llama-2 base\",\n1014\t            \"80.2%\",\n1015\t            \"100%\",\n1016\t            \"LM pretraining provides separability, not VLA training\"\n1017\t          ],\n1018\t          [\n1019\t            \"Untrained (random)\",\n1020\t            \"100%\",\n1021\t            \"82%\",\n1022\t            \"Even random features separate 10 classes at L1\"\n1023\t          ],\n1024\t          [\n1025\t            \"Image mean\",\n1026\t            \"10%\",\n1027\t            \"10%\",\n1028\t            \"Causal mask guarantee, not finding\"\n1029\t          ]\n1030\t        ]\n1031\t      }\n1032\t    ],\n1033\t    \"figures\": [],\n1034\t    \"analysis\": \"C1 的 experimental framework 是 reframe 后的 primary contribution。但 cross-instruction\\nclassification 作为 framework demo 的问题：10-way on 4096d 太 easy，不 demonstrate\\nframework 在 harder settings 下的 value。需要更 challenging classification tasks\\n或 fine-grained metrics 来 justify framework utility。\\n\\n\\n数据完整。Worst 档下 C1 被彻底降级：\\n\\\"10-way classification on 4096-dim features 是 trivially easy。Untrained (random init)\\nL1 也达到 100%——random projection 就能分离 10 个 class。你的 LOOCV 只在 untrained deep layers\\n下降到 85%——这不是 'training improves routing' 而是 'random weights corrupt signal in deep layers'。\\n\\nImage mean = 10% at all layers 是 causal mask guarantee 不是 finding。你自己承认了。\\n\\n三条件对比（trained flat 100%, llama2base saturates L5, untrained decays to 82%）的\\ninterpretation 也被质疑：'trained L1=99.6% vs llama2base L1=80.2%' 看起来像 'training\\ncreates immediate routing'，但 D090 证明 L1 heads 来自 base model 而非 training。\\n那 99.6% vs 80.2% 的差异可能只反映 VLA fine-tuning 后 feature quality 提升（action-relevant\\nfeatures are more linearly separable）而非 routing reorganization。\\n\\n贡献在 methodology（factorial design + 4 methods）而非 findings。但 methodology 贡献在\\nCoRL 通常只值 weak accept——CoRL 偏好 systems + behavioral results。\\\"\\n\"\n1035\t  },\n1036\t  {\n1037\t    \"name\": \"Head Ablation and Specificity Controls\",\n1038\t    \"description\": \"L1 attention head ablation 实验套件 — 验证 instruction-dominant heads 的功能特异性\",\n1039\t    \"results\": {\n1040\t      \"baseline_r2_L13\": 0.676,\n1041\t      \"ablate_24_instr_r2_L13\": 0.676,\n1042\t      \"ablate_24_random_r2_L13\": 0.664,\n1043\t      \"random_24_z_score\": -2.73,\n1044\t      \"specificity_ratio\": 1.08,\n1045\t      \"instruction_d\": 0.651,\n1046\t      \"random_24_d\": 0.601,\n1047\t      \"image_24_d\": 0.58,\n1048\t      \"gt_error_delta_mse\": -0.001\n1049\t    },\n1050\t    \"tables\": [\n1051\t      {\n1052\t        \"title\": \"Head Ablation: No Functional Specificity\",\n1053\t        \"columns\": [\n1054\t          \"Ablation Group\",\n1055\t          \"24h d\",\n1056\t          \"Per-head d\",\n1057\t          \"GT ΔMSE\",\n1058\t          \"Worst Reading\"\n1059\t        ],\n1060\t        \"rows\": [\n1061\t          [\n1062\t            \"Instr-dominant 24\",\n1063\t            \"0.651\",\n1064\t            \"0.027\",\n1065\t            \"-0.001 (p=0.52)\",\n1066\t            \"Changes direction, not quality\"\n1067\t          ],\n1068\t          [\n1069\t            \"Random 24 (avg)\",\n1070\t            \"0.601\",\n1071\t            \"0.025\",\n1072\t            \"similar\",\n1073\t            \"Any 24 heads produce similar effect\"\n1074\t          ],\n1075\t          [\n1076\t            \"Image-dominant 24\",\n1077\t            \"0.580\",\n1078\t            \"0.024\",\n1079\t            \"similar\",\n1080\t            \"No group specificity\"\n1081\t          ],\n1082\t          [\n1083\t            \"Control 8 (random)\",\n1084\t            \"0.410\",\n1085\t            \"0.051\",\n1086\t            \"similar\",\n1087\t            \"Per-head effect LARGER in control\"\n1088\t          ]\n1089\t        ]\n1090\t      }\n1091\t    ],\n1092\t    \"figures\": [],\n1093\t    \"analysis\": \"Head ablation suite is worst tier's most damaging evidence against CF sensitivity as\\nfunctional routing. ΔMSE≈0 + specificity ratio 1.08x together argue that instruction\\nrouting (as measured by attention head dominance) has no disproportionate functional role.\\nFramework reframe 很难 rescue this——the framework's own ablation tool reveals that\\nthe effect it detected (instruction routing) is not functionally specific.\\n\\n\\n数据已完成。Worst 档下 ablation 结果被严厉解读：\\n\\n(1) Specificity ratio = 1.08x 极弱：\\\"instruction-dominant 24 heads 的 per-head effect\\n不比 random 24 heads 大多少（z=-2.73 但 effect size tiny）。任何 24/32 heads ablation\\n产生 similar or larger R² increase（random 24 mean delta = 0.077 > instruction 24 delta = 0.042）。\\nInstruction-dominant heads 不是 special——they're 75% of all heads，removing ANY 75%\\nof heads produces similar effects。\\\"\\n\\n(2) ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth 是 worst tier 最致命的 finding：\\\"你 ablate 24 instruction-dominant\\nheads，action outputs change direction (d=0.65) 但 ground-truth error 不变（ΔMSE=-0.001, p=0.52）。\\n这意味着 instruction routing 对 action quality 无影响——perturbation 改变 output 方向\\n但不改变 output 质量。这直接证明 CF sensitivity 缺乏 functional significance。\\n如果移除 75% 的 'instruction routing heads' 对 action quality 无影响，\\n那 instruction routing 在 action generation 中可能是 redundant mechanism。\\\"\\n\\n(3) Information-computation dissociation 解读在 worst tier 下被反转：论文 cite Hewitt & Liang 2019\\n作为 \\\"ΔMSE≈0 is expected under dissociation\\\"，但 reviewer 说：\\n\\\"Hewitt & Liang 的 point 是 probe results don't prove representation is functionally used。\\n你在用他们的 framework 来 excuse 你的 negative result。ΔMSE≈0 doesn't support 'routing\\nmodulates without degrading'——it supports 'routing doesn't matter for output quality'。\\\"\\n\"\n1094\t  },\n1095\t  {\n1096\t    \"name\": \"Counterfactual Token Overlap and Trajectory-Level Analysis\",\n1097\t    \"description\": \"CF perturbation 的 token overlap, trajectory-level d, 和 ΔMSE 扩展分析\",\n1098\t    \"results\": {\n1099\t      \"token_overlap_spearman\": 1.0,\n1100\t      \"empty_d_token\": 0.968,\n1101\t      \"empty_d_trajectory\": 3.438,\n1102\t      \"wrong_d_token\": 0.844,\n1103\t      \"wrong_d_trajectory\": 3.798,\n1104\t      \"shuffled_d_token\": 0.625,\n1105\t      \"shuffled_d_trajectory\": 2.595,\n1106\t      \"para_d_token\": 0.697,\n1107\t      \"para_d_trajectory\": 2.131,\n1108\t      \"inflation_factor_mean\": 0.245,\n1109\t      \"gt_mse_original\": 0.498,\n1110\t      \"gt_mse_top24_ablated\": 0.497,\n1111\t      \"gt_mse_delta\": -0.001\n1112\t    },\n1113\t    \"tables\": [\n1114\t      {\n1115\t        \"title\": \"Token Overlap → Cohen's d: Surface-Level Sensitivity\",\n1116\t        \"columns\": [\n1117\t          \"Perturbation\",\n1118\t          \"Token Novelty\",\n1119\t          \"Token d\",\n1120\t          \"Traj d\",\n1121\t          \"Worst Reading\"\n1122\t        ],\n1123\t        \"rows\": [\n1124\t          [\n1125\t            \"empty\",\n1126\t            \"1.0\",\n1127\t            \"0.968\",\n1128\t            \"3.438\",\n1129\t            \"Max novelty → max effect: lexical, not semantic\"\n1130\t          ],\n1131\t          [\n1132\t            \"wrong\",\n1133\t            \"0.83\",\n1134\t            \"0.844\",\n1135\t            \"3.798\",\n1136\t            \"High novelty → high effect\"\n1137\t          ],\n1138\t          [\n1139\t            \"paraphrased\",\n1140\t            \"0.47\",\n1141\t            \"0.697\",\n1142\t            \"2.131\",\n1143\t            \"Low novelty → low effect\"\n1144\t          ],\n1145\t          [\n1146\t            \"shuffled\",\n1147\t            \"0.0\",\n1148\t            \"0.625\",\n1149\t            \"2.595\",\n1150\t            \"Zero novelty but positional change → moderate\"\n1151\t          ]\n1152\t        ]\n1153\t      }\n1154\t    ],\n1155\t    \"figures\": [],\n1156\t    \"analysis\": \"ρ=1.0 token-novelty/d correlation is worst-tier's strongest argument that CF sensitivity\\nmeasures lexical sensitivity rather than semantic routing. Framework reframe has no good\\ncounter — the framework's own analysis reveals CF is surface-level. Could argue \\\"shuffled\\nsame tokens different order still produces d=0.63\\\" as evidence of positional sensitivity\\nbeyond pure lexical, but this is weak defense.\\n\\n\\n数据已完成。Worst 档下 token overlap analysis 被反过来用：\\n\\n\\\"Spearman ρ=1.0 between token novelty and Cohen's d 说明 CF sensitivity 完全由\\nlexical/positional distance 驱动，不是 semantic distance。Empty（最大 token novelty）→\\nlargest d，shuffled（same tokens, different order）→ moderate d，paraphrased（high overlap）→\\nsmallest d。这不是 'the model understands instruction semantics'——这是 'the model responds\\nto surface-level token changes'。任何 autoregressive language model 都会如此。\\\"\\n\\nTrajectory-level d（2.1-3.8）远大于 token-level d（0.6-0.97）——inflation factor ~4x。\\nWorst reviewer：\\\"trajectory-level inflation 说明 per-timestep effects 累积——这不是\\n'stronger evidence of routing' 而是 'autocorrelation amplification'。每个 timestep\\n的小 perturbation 通过 temporal autocorrelation 累积成大 trajectory difference，\\n这是 dynamical systems 的 trivial property 不是 routing evidence。\\\"\\n\\nGT MSE unchanged（0.498 vs 0.497）再次确认 CF perturbation 不影响 action quality。\\n\"\n1157\t  },\n1158\t  {\n1159\t    \"name\": \"D090 Synthesis: What VLA Training Actually Contributes\",\n1160\t    \"description\": \"综合评估：D090 后论文的 residual contribution\",\n1161\t    \"results\": {\n1162\t      \"training_induced_effects\": [\n1163\t        \"R² exit collapse (VLM→VLA only)\",\n1164\t        \"CF sensitivity (unfair baselines)\"\n1165\t      ],\n1166\t      \"base_model_effects\": [\n1167\t        \"L1 head count\",\n1168\t        \"deep-layer probe stability\"\n1169\t      ],\n1170\t      \"removed_contributions\": [\n1171\t        \"L1 routing gradient\",\n1172\t        \"attention bookend pattern (entry component)\"\n1173\t      ],\n1174\t      \"remaining_unique\": \"1-2 effects, both with caveats\",\n1175\t      \"reviewer_avg_score\": [\n1176\t        4.0,\n1177\t        5.5\n1178\t      ],\n1179\t      \"strong_reject_count\": [\n1180\t        1,\n1181\t        2\n1182\t      ],\n1183\t      \"accept_probability\": [\n1184\t        0.05,\n1185\t        0.2\n1186\t      ],\n1187\t      \"claims_surviving\": [\n1188\t        0.5,\n1189\t        1.5\n1190\t      ]\n1191\t    },\n1192\t    \"tables\": [\n1193\t      {\n1194\t        \"title\": \"Worst-Tier Score Prediction\",\n1195\t        \"columns\": [\n1196\t          \"Reviewer\",\n1197\t          \"Score\",\n1198\t          \"Primary Concern\",\n1199\t          \"Verdict\"\n1200\t        ],\n1201\t        \"rows\": [\n1202\t          [\n1203\t            \"R1 (behavioral)\",\n1204\t            \"4\",\n1205\t            \"No closed-loop validation; CoRL is robotics venue\",\n1206\t            \"Reject\"\n1207\t          ],\n1208\t          [\n1209\t            \"R2 (methodology)\",\n1210\t            \"6\",\n1211\t            \"Framework solid; findings thin but honest\",\n1212\t            \"Weak Accept\"\n1213\t          ],\n1214\t          [\n1215\t            \"R3 (generalizability)\",\n1216\t            \"4\",\n1217\t            \"Magnitude variance; incommensurable baselines; over-qualified claims\",\n1218\t            \"Reject\"\n1219\t          ],\n1220\t          [\n1221\t            \"Mean\",\n1222\t            \"4.67\",\n1223\t            \"2 reject + 1 weak accept\",\n1224\t            \"Likely Reject\"\n1225\t          ]\n1226\t        ]\n1227\t      },\n1228\t      {\n1229\t        \"title\": \"Reframe Impact on Scores\",\n1230\t        \"columns\": [\n1231\t          \"Reframe Element\",\n1232\t          \"Score Impact\",\n1233\t          \"Which Reviewer\"\n1234\t        ],\n1235\t        \"rows\": [\n1236\t          [\n1237\t            \"C1 framework as primary contribution\",\n1238\t            \"+1 for R2 only\",\n1239\t            \"R2: 6→7\"\n1240\t          ],\n1241\t          [\n1242\t            \"D090 as framework capability demo\",\n1243\t            \"+0.5 for R2\",\n1244\t            \"R2 already sympathetic\"\n1245\t          ],\n1246\t          [\n1247\t            \"Exit collapse as diagnostic\",\n1248\t            \"0 for R1/R3\",\n1249\t            \"Doesn't address behavioral gap\"\n1250\t          ],\n1251\t          [\n1252\t            \"Roadmap for closed-loop future work\",\n1253\t            \"+0.5 for R1 maybe\",\n1254\t            \"R1 may soften to 4.5\"\n1255\t          ],\n1256\t          [\n1257\t            \"Net after reframe\",\n1258\t            \"Mean ~5.0\",\n1259\t            \"Still borderline reject\"\n1260\t          ]\n1261\t        ]\n1262\t      }\n1263\t    ],\n1264\t    \"figures\": [],\n1265\t    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 核心判定：论文 honest analysis (D090) + thorough controls (D100) 是 scientifically\\ncommendable 但 strategically devastating。每个 defense 实验排除了一个 confound 但同时削弱了\\ncontribution scope。D090 证明 L1 routing 不是训练效果；D100 证明 exit collapse 不是 generic\\nfinetuning 但仍被视为 trivial；ΔMSE≈0 证明 ablation 不影响 quality 但被解读为 \\\"routing\\ndoesn't functionally matter\\\"。\\n\\nReframe 路径：diagnostic framework + honest empirical characterization。Accept probability\\n0.05-0.20 range。需要 AC 认可 methodology contribution 的 standalone value 才有机会。\\n关键 rebuttal material：(1) representation engineering literature 论证 representational\\nanalysis 的独立价值，(2) exit collapse as VLM→VLA binary diagnostic 的 concrete use case\\n（判断 pretraining checkpoint 是否完成 VLA transition），(3) framework reusability 的\\n具体 demonstration（how others can apply it to new VLAs）。\\n\\nD090 后 contribution audit 在 worst tier 下：\\n\\nTraining-induced（retained but weakened）:\\n- R² exit collapse：6/6 VLM→VLA, 0/4 VLA→VLA — clean binary。D100 排除 NLP confound。\\n  但 worst reviewer 视为 \\\"trivially expected transition artifact\\\"。\\n- CF sensitivity：d≥0.45 in all trained settings。但 incommensurable baselines（5/7 pairs），\\n  ρ=1.0 token-novelty correlation（surface-level），ΔMSE≈0（no functional consequence）。\\n\\nBase-model-dependent（removed from contribution）:\\n- L1 head count：Phi-3 32/32 untrained, NORA 13/16 untrained — not training-induced。\\n- Deep-layer stability：Llama-2 base also stable（100% L5+）— from LM pretraining。\\n\\nReviewer score prediction:\\n- R1（expects behavioral results）：4/10 — \\\"descriptive analysis without actionable insight,\\n  CoRL expects at minimum open-loop policy evaluation.\\\"\\n- R2（appreciates methodology）：6/10 — \\\"framework is solid and systematic, cross-architecture\\n  validation is thorough engineering. But findings are thin after D090 self-critique.\\\"\\n- R3（generalizability focus）：4/10 — \\\"exit collapse magnitude 4.4x range within VLM→VLA,\\n  CF baselines incommensurable. Claims are over-qualified to the point of being unfalsifiable.\\\"\\nMean: 4.67. Strong reject: 0-1. Accept probability: 0.10-0.20.\\n\\nReframe 能做的最大提升：如果 C1 framework 成功 pitch 为 primary contribution（\\\"first\\nsystematic VLA profiling toolkit\\\"），R2 可能升到 7，但 R1/R3 不变——\\n结果 mean 5.0，borderline reject。需要 AC 同情才有机会。\\n\"\n1266\t  }\n1267\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49e11fde-ca39-4b97-b0e5-e979be22c1ed","uuid":"bb61fb8d-e0b8-4796-ba99-45c511933561","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:10:21.924Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260527T022433/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SigLIP+Projector RSA vs Full VLA vs DINO\",\n    \"description\": \"SigLIP+Projector RSA 对比 Full VLA 和 DINO，证明 action-relevant 结构源自 frozen vision encoder\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"siglip_projector_rsa\": 0.615,\n      \"trained_with_inst_rsa\": 0.488,\n      \"untrained_with_inst_rsa\": 0.485,\n      \"dino_rsa\": 0.388,\n      \"llm_degradation_delta\": 0.127\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"SigLIP RSA Scope Limitation (Worst-Tier)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Source\",\n          \"RSA\",\n          \"Architecture Coverage\",\n          \"Worst Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SigLIP+Proj\",\n            \"0.615\",\n            \"OpenVLA only\",\n            \"Cannot generalize to other VLA encoders\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA trained\",\n            \"0.488\",\n            \"OpenVLA only\",\n            \"Llama-2-specific LLM degradation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA untrained\",\n            \"0.485\",\n            \"OpenVLA only\",\n            \"Random-init Llama-2 specific\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DINO\",\n            \"0.388\",\n            \"Standalone\",\n            \"Reference baseline, unaffected\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Framework reframe 下此实验从 C1 core evidence 降为 Section 4.1 case study。价值在于 demonstrate\\nframework 的 encoder-LLM decomposition 能力，而非 claim 本身。Reviewer 不会因此给分但也不会因此扣分——\\nneutral contribution in worst tier。但 LLM degradation finding 可能被用来攻击论文 motivation 本身。\\n\\n\\n数据已完成不变。在 worst 档下，此实验仅覆盖 OpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP encoder。Reviewer 攻击路线：\\n\\\"SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 是 OpenVLA-specific frozen encoder 的观察。TracVLA 用 Phi-3-Vision encoder，\\nNORA 用 InternViT——你们没测这些 encoder 的 RSA。单架构 encoder analysis 无法 claim architecture-independent。\\\"\\nLLM degradation（0.615→0.488）本身被视为 \\\"trivially expected—— LLM 的 intermediate processing 当然会\\n改变 representation geometry，这不是 finding 而是 definition。\\\" 在 diagnostic framework reframe 下，\\n此实验降为 \\\"framework 在 OpenVLA 上的 case study\\\"——不再是 core contribution。更致命的是，Reviewer 会用\\n这个实验反过来攻击论文 motivation：\\\"如果 frozen encoder 已经提供了最好的 action-relevant structure（RSA=0.615），\\n而 LLM processing 只是 degrade 它（到 0.488），那为什么要研究 LLM 内部的 instruction routing？问题不在 routing\\n而在 LLM 设计本身——你应该研究如何让 LLM 不 degrade encoder output。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DINO baseline RSA\",\n    \"description\": \"Standalone vision model 参照基线\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dino_rsa\": 0.388,\n      \"dino_action_R2\": 0.687,\n      \"dino_subtask_auc\": 0.972\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 下 DINO baseline 被用来论证整篇论文的 premise 可疑：如果 vision alone 足够好，\\ninstruction routing research 的 practical relevance 被严重削弱。Framework reframe 可以\\nacknowledge 但无法完全化解这个攻击。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下 DINO 的角色被 weaponize：R²=0.687 对比 VLA 训练后的 exit R² drop。Reviewer：\\n\\\"DINO（self-supervised, 无 language, 无 action training）的 action probe R²=0.687 已经很高，\\n说明 action prediction 主要是 visual task。你们声称的 VLA 训练重组 instruction routing，但如果一个\\n纯视觉模型无需任何 instruction 就能达到 R²=0.687，instruction routing 的 practical value 是什么？\\n这反而证明了 Grant et al. 2026 的 visual dominance finding——instructions 在 VLA 中可能根本不重要。\\\"\\nDINO subtask AUC=0.972 进一步强化这个论点——task progress 几乎完全可从 visual features 预测，\\n无需 instruction information。这直接攻击论文研究 instruction routing 的 premise。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\",\n    \"description\": \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output 到 LLM 各层的变换轨迹\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"proj_rsa\": 0.615,\n      \"trained_peak_rsa\": 0.488,\n      \"trained_peak_layer\": 9,\n      \"untrained_peak_rsa\": 0.485,\n      \"untrained_peak_layer\": 12,\n      \"proj_to_l1_drop\": 0.13,\n      \"inverted_u_trained\": true,\n      \"inverted_u_untrained\": true,\n      \"rise_phase_delta\": 0.016\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"RSA Inverted-U Architecture Coverage\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"RSA Per-Layer Done?\",\n          \"Pattern\",\n          \"Worst Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B)\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"Inverted-U\",\n            \"Only confirmed case, CKA reversal undermines\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TracVLA (Phi-3-mini)\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Unknown\",\n            \"Cannot claim generalization\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B)\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Unknown\",\n            \"Cannot claim generalization\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Inverted-U 成为 C3 observation 的核心证据但被 metric-dependence 严重削弱。\\nFramework reframe 下可保留为 \\\"framework reveals metric-dependent patterns\\\"\\n但这同时 undermine 了 framework 发现的 authority——如果换个 metric 结论就变，framework 的可靠性如何？\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下 inverted-U 只在 OpenVLA (Llama-2) 上验证过，TracVLA/NORA 的 RSA per-layer\\ncurve 从未做过。CKA 在 plan_009 中反转了 RSA ordering（untrained > trained），使 RSA metric 的\\nauthority 受损。Rise phase Δρ=0.016 极小（CI 可能 includes 0），reviewer 会指出：\\n\\\"你声称 training shifts RSA peak from L0 to L12，但 rise phase 只有 0.016 ρ——这在 noise level 内。\\n如果 CKA 不支持 inverted-U，你不能 claim 这是 robust pattern——这是 metric-specific artifact。\\\"\\n在 CoRL（robotics venue），per-layer RSA curve 被视为 \\\"interesting visualization but not\\ncontribution\\\"——reviewer 期望功能性验证而非几何观察。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Output head analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"SigLIP+projector frozen 确认, LLM 权重变化不传导到表征\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"vision_projector_cos_sim\": 1.0,\n      \"llm_rel_change_mean\": 1.316,\n      \"llm_rel_change_range\": [\n        1.22,\n        1.37\n      ],\n      \"head_vs_llm_ratio\": 1.12,\n      \"shallow_adaptation_gate\": \"FAIL\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"贡献接近零。Framework reframe 下可作为 \\\"component attribution capability\\\" 的 one-sentence\\nmention。不值得独立分析。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下此实验被视为 trivial verification：\\\"OpenVLA 代码 freeze 了 vision encoder，\\n你只是验证了代码做了它该做的事。cos_sim=1.0 不是 finding，是 implementation check。\\\"\\nLLM 权重均匀分布（1.22-1.37）也不 surprising——\\\"random init vs pretrained 的差异当然大且均匀，\\n这是 comparing random weights to structured weights，不是 analyzing fine-tuning effects。\\n你的 caveat 自己也说了：comparison is pretrained Llama + fine-tune vs random init，\\n所以 differences dominated by pretrained vs random，not by VLA training.\\\"\\n在 8-page limit 下，worst tier 建议此实验压缩为半段或移到 appendix。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks 系统验证\",\n    \"description\": \"系统性验证 trained ≈ untrained 表征结构\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"trained_untrained_rsa_delta\": 0.003,\n      \"trained_untrained_r2_delta\": 0.015,\n      \"cka_ordering_reversal\": true,\n      \"all_methods_show_vla_gt_dino\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"6 Methods Under Worst-Tier Reinterpretation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Trained-Untrained Δ\",\n          \"Worst Reviewer Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RSA (geometric)\",\n            \"0.003\",\n            \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"R² action probe\",\n            \"+0.015\",\n            \"Marginal: within noise\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CKA (global)\",\n            \"-0.006\",\n            \"REVERSAL: undermines RSA narrative\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Action probe (MLP)\",\n            \"+0.045\",\n            \"Small routing effect, not surprising\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Delta probe\",\n            \"+0.011\",\n            \"Same encoder → similar structure\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Classification\",\n            \"+0.001\",\n            \"Trivially easy for both conditions\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"6 methods consistency 从 \\\"strong evidence for trained ≈ untrained\\\" 降为\\n\\\"thorough but unsurprising verification of a structurally predicted outcome\\\"。\\nCKA reversal 使 \\\"all methods consistent\\\" claim 不成立。Framework reframe 下\\n唯一残余价值：demonstrate framework 的 multi-method coverage capability。\\n\\n\\nOrphaned 但子实验（RSA, R², CKA, action probe, delta probe, classification）均已完成。\\nWorst 档下 trained ≈ untrained 被视为 \\\"trivially expected under frozen encoder\\\"。\\nReviewer：\\\"frozen SigLIP+projector 输出相同 L0 features，LLM fine-tuning 只改变 weights\\n而非 input distribution——所以 intermediate layer representations naturally similar。\\n你用 6 种方法验证一个 structurally guaranteed result，这不是 thoroughness 而是 over-verification。\\\"\\nCKA ordering reversal 进一步削弱 multi-method consistency narrative——6 methods 中 CKA\\n反转了 RSA，说明 \\\"consistency\\\" 是 cherry-picked（只 consistent 在某些 metrics 下）。\\nWorst reviewer 总结：\\\"这些实验证明了 VLA > DINO 但 trained ≈ untrained——\\n前者 expected（LLM 有 4096d features vs DINO 1024d），后者 也 expected（same encoder）。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Instruction ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"去掉 instruction text 测 RSA 变化\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"delta_with_vs_no_inst\": 0.004,\n      \"gate_judgment\": \"FAIL — instruction 无影响 on RSA\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 下从 C3 evidence 降为 \\\"confirms structural prediction, not finding\\\"。\\nFramework reframe 下可作为 \\\"sanity check\\\" 一句带过，不占独立段落。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下被视为 tautological sanity check：image token RSA 在 causal mask 下\\n不受 instruction tokens 影响是 structural guarantee，不是 empirical finding。\\nReviewer：\\\"你在 C1 里承认 causal mask 使 image tokens 看不到 instructions，\\n然后在 plan_006 里'发现' image RSA 不受 instructions 影响——这是验证了你自己的前提假设。\\nΔ=0.004 是 noise，不是 small effect——effect 在结构上不可能存在。\\n这 0.5 页可以省掉或用一句话带过。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"2×2 matrix (training × instruction)\",\n    \"description\": \"四条件全收敛验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"trained_with_inst\": 0.488,\n      \"trained_no_inst\": 0.489,\n      \"untrained_with_inst\": 0.485,\n      \"untrained_no_inst\": 0.48,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_includes_0\": true,\n      \"training_effect\": 0.003,\n      \"instruction_effect\": 0.004\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"2×2 Matrix as Expected Null (Worst-Tier)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"RSA\",\n          \"Reviewer Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Trained + Inst\",\n            \"0.488\",\n            \"Expected: frozen encoder dominates\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Trained - Inst\",\n            \"0.489\",\n            \"Expected: causal mask blocks\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Untrained + Inst\",\n            \"0.485\",\n            \"Expected: same encoder\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Untrained - Inst\",\n            \"0.480\",\n            \"Expected: both factors null\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Framework reframe 下 2×2 matrix 的价值从 \\\"finding\\\" 转为 \\\"exemplar of factorial\\ndesign capability\\\"——可复用性贡献，但在 CoRL 不计高分。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。Worst 档下 2×2 null result 被视为 \\\"expected outcome of frozen encoder + causal mask\\\"。\\nReviewer：\\\"你的 2×2 factorial design 是好的 experimental methodology，但它发现了 predicted null——\\nboth factors (training, instruction) have no effect on image token RSA 因为 (1) encoder frozen,\\n(2) causal mask blocks instruction→image. 好的 experimental design + expected null result\\n= methodology paper contribution, not empirical contribution。如果这是 methodology paper\\n那 ok，但你 pitch 的是 empirical findings about VLA routing。\\\"\\n四条件收敛到 0.48-0.49 band 进一步证实 RSA 对 image tokens 是 ceiling+floor bounded by encoder quality。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Random instruction control\",\n    \"description\": \"随机/无意义 instruction 替代验证 RSA 不受 instruction content 影响\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"normal_rsa\": 0.489,\n      \"random_rsa\": 0.484,\n      \"shuffled_rsa\": 0.483,\n      \"empty_rsa\": 0.472,\n      \"max_absolute_delta\": 0.017,\n      \"instruction_invariant\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"006/007/008 三合一压缩为半段。Framework reframe 下仅作为 \\\"invariance verification\\\"\\nmethodology demo。在 worst tier 下浪费篇幅的风险 > 贡献。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。与 plan_006/007 同一逻辑链——causal mask 使 image token RSA 对 instruction content\\n天然不变。Worst reviewer：\\\"你用了三个 experiments（006/007/008）验证同一个 structurally guaranteed\\nnull result。Normal/random/shuffled/empty 全在 ±0.02 内不是 finding，是 noise around a\\nguaranteed null。这占了论文篇幅但不增加 contribution。在 8 页限制下，三个实验应压缩为 1 段 sanity check。\\\"\\n更刻薄的 reviewer：\\\"spending 3 experiments on 'image tokens don't see instruction tokens'\\nsuggests the authors don't fully understand their own architecture's causal mask structure.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA verification\",\n    \"description\": \"CKA 指标验证 RSA 发现的 metric robustness\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"linear_cka_ordering\": \"untrained > trained > projector > DINO\",\n      \"rsa_ordering\": \"projector > trained > untrained > DINO\",\n      \"ordering_reversal\": true,\n      \"last_preaction_cka\": 0.127\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Metric Ordering Reversal (Worst-Tier Authority Crisis)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Ordering\",\n          \"Implication\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RSA (geometric)\",\n            \"SigLIP > T > U > DINO\",\n            \"Training degrades geometry\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CKA (global)\",\n            \"U > T > SigLIP > DINO\",\n            \"Training preserves/improves structure\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"R² (functional)\",\n            \"T_lastpre > DINO ≈ Proj > T_img > U\",\n            \"Training enables routing\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Reviewer question\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Framework credibility if metrics disagree?\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA dissociation 在 worst tier 下是 double-edged：可以包装为 \\\"why we need multi-metric\\nframework\\\" 但同时 undermines 所有 single-metric conclusions。Exit collapse 只在 R²\\n下明显——如果 CKA 下不 collapse，reviewer 要求 \\\"architecture-independent\\\" 必须\\n\\\"metric-independent\\\"，否则 claim 降级。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。CKA-RSA dissociation 在 worst 档下变得 doubly 致命。\\n第一层攻击（保持不变）：\\\"如果 CKA 说 untrained > trained 而 RSA 说 trained > untrained，\\n那哪个 metric 才反映 'action-relevant information'？你选了 RSA 来讲 story，但另一个\\nequally principled metric 给出相反结论。这不是 metric dissociation finding——\\n这是 your conclusions are metric-dependent 的 admission。\\\"\\n第二层攻击（D095 升级后更致命）：\\\"你们现在 claim R² exit collapse 是跨架构一致的\\nVLM→VLA signature。但 R² 本身是 functional metric（probe-based），RSA 是 geometric metric，\\nCKA 是 kernel-based metric。如果不同 metrics 给不同结论，你凭什么用 R² 的 exit collapse\\n而不是 CKA 的 no-collapse 来 claim 'architecture-independent signature'？\\n你的 framework 应该 reconcile 这些 metrics 而不是 pick 对你有利的那个。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark 扩展\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 benchmark（LIBERO-Spatial）交叉验证\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"trained_image_mean_peak_R2\": 0.696,\n      \"trained_image_mean_peak_layer\": 13,\n      \"trained_last_preaction_peak_R2\": 0.675,\n      \"trained_last_preaction_peak_layer\": 21,\n      \"untrained_image_mean_peak_R2\": 0.673,\n      \"untrained_last_preaction_peak_R2\": 0.635,\n      \"trained_vs_untrained_delta_imgmean\": 0.023,\n      \"trained_vs_untrained_delta_lastpre\": 0.04,\n      \"bootstrap_p\": 0.001\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Benchmark Comparison (OpenVLA Only)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Delta (imgmean best-vs-best)\",\n          \"Delta (lastpre best-vs-best)\",\n          \"Worst Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LIBERO-Goal\",\n            \"0.015\",\n            \"0.069\",\n            \"Moderate; only architecture tested\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LIBERO-Spatial\",\n            \"0.023\",\n            \"0.040\",\n            \"Small; confirms VLA→VLA transition minimal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Implication\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Within-arch replication, not cross-arch validation\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cross-benchmark replication 有价值但不解决 cross-architecture gap。D102 framing 下\\nsmall delta 是 expected（VLA→VLA），但 reviewer 会用此攻击：\\\"如果进一步 finetuning\\n不 substantially change representations，studying finetuning effects 的意义何在？\\\"\\n\\n\\n数据已完成。Worst 档下此实验是 within-architecture cross-benchmark（仍是 OpenVLA），\\n不解决 RC4 的 cross-architecture concern。Reviewer：\\\"从 LIBERO-Goal 换到 LIBERO-Spatial\\n只是换了 task suite 不是换了 VLA 架构——这不回答 'does it generalize across architectures'。\\\"\\nSpatial 的 trained-untrained delta（best-vs-best）=0.023（imgmean）/ 0.040（lastpre）\\n小于 Goal 的 0.015/0.069。退一步看，R² exit collapse 在 D102 更新后被重新定义为\\nVLM→VLA transition effect——但 LIBERO-Spatial 和 Goal 都用同一个 OpenVLA checkpoint（已是 VLA），\\n所以 trained vs untrained（OXE vs LIBERO-finetuned）的 delta 本就该小（VLA→VLA transition）。\\n这与 D102 结论一致但在 worst tier 下被解读为 \\\"further fine-tuning doesn't change much\\n= fine-tuning doesn't matter much = your study of fine-tuning effects is studying something trivial。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Full-layer R² scan\",\n    \"description\": \"33 layers × 2 conditions × 2 aggregations = 132 probes 的 R² 全层扫描\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"trained_image_mean_peak\": {\n        \"layer\": 8,\n        \"R2\": 0.655\n      },\n      \"trained_last_preaction_peak\": {\n        \"layer\": 13,\n        \"R2\": 0.678\n      },\n      \"untrained_image_mean_peak\": {\n        \"layer\": 0,\n        \"R2\": 0.64\n      },\n      \"untrained_last_preaction_peak\": {\n        \"layer\": 32,\n        \"R2\": 0.609\n      },\n      \"trained_exit_R2_lastpre\": 0.422,\n      \"untrained_exit_R2_lastpre\": 0.545,\n      \"exit_collapse_delta_lastpre\": 0.256,\n      \"best_vs_best_lastpre_delta\": 0.069,\n      \"best_vs_best_lastpre_p\": 0.0001\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"R² Exit Collapse with D100/D102 Context (Worst-Tier)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"Peak R²\",\n          \"Exit R²\",\n          \"Δ\",\n          \"Worst Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"VLA trained\",\n            \"0.678 (L13)\",\n            \"0.422 (L32)\",\n            \"0.256\",\n            \"Action head 'consumes' info — trivially expected\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OXE untrained\",\n            \"0.609 (L32)\",\n            \"0.609 (L32)\",\n            \"0.000\",\n            \"No exit collapse — consistent with VLA→VLA null\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-2-chat (D100)\",\n            \"0.156 (all)\",\n            \"0.156 (all)\",\n            \"0.000\",\n            \"NLP: flat noise floor, no action info anywhere\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random init\",\n            \"0.640 (L0)\",\n            \"~0 (L10-L13)\",\n            \"pathological\",\n            \"Not valid control — random weights meaningless\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"D100 NLP control 排除了 generic fine-tuning confound，这是论文的防御性胜利。但 worst reviewer\\n的 next-level 攻击——exit collapse 是 \\\"action consumption\\\" 而非 \\\"routing mechanism\\\"——\\n仍然 stands without behavioral validation。Framework reframe 可以 acknowledge 这个区分\\n并 position exit collapse 为 \\\"diagnostic indicator of action training stage\\\" 而非 \\\"mechanistic finding\\\"。\\n\\n\\n数据不变（OpenVLA 单架构）。这是 R² exit collapse 的源头实验。D100 NLP control 已排除\\ngeneric fine-tuning confound（Llama-2-chat ΔR²=0.000），D102 将其定义为 VLM→VLA transition effect。\\n但 worst-tier reviewer 反转 D100/D102：\\n\\\"D100 证明 NLP finetuning 不产生 exit collapse——好。但这只说明 exit collapse 需要 action training，\\n不说明它有 functional significance。VLM→VLA transition 当然改变 exit layer——action head 需要从\\nexit layer decode 7-DOF actions，这不是 routing 'discovery' 而是 'the model learned to produce actions\\nand the last layer reflects that'。你的 R² probe 测量的是 Ridge regression 从 hidden states 预测 actions\\n的能力——exit layer R² 下降只是说明 action-relevant information 被 'consumed' by action decoding，\\n不是被 'discarded' by routing mechanism。这是 trivially expected under any encoder-decoder framework。\\\"\\nWorst reviewer 要求 behavioral evidence：如果 exit collapse 是 functional routing，\\nablating exit-layer representations 应该 disproportionately affect task performance——但这从未被测试。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CLIP-ViT pretraining control\",\n    \"description\": \"CLIP ViT-L 替代 SigLIP 区分 VL pretraining vs encoder quality\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"clip_rsa\": 0.557,\n      \"clip_R2\": 0.587,\n      \"dino_cls_rsa\": 0.692,\n      \"dino_cls_R2\": 0.634,\n      \"projector_R2\": 0.63,\n      \"vl_pretraining_not_superior\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Encoder Quality vs Language Supervision\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"RSA\",\n          \"R²\",\n          \"Has Language?\",\n          \"Worst Implication\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DINO cls\",\n            \"0.692\",\n            \"0.634\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Best in both — language supervision unnecessary\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SigLIP+Proj\",\n            \"0.615\",\n            \"0.630\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"VL pretraining inferior to DINO\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CLIP ViT-L\",\n            \"0.557\",\n            \"0.587\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"Worst VL encoder\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Implication\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"Language supervision may hurt encoder quality\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CLIP control 结果在 worst tier 下不仅否定 VL pretraining superiority，更挑战整篇论文的\\nmotivation。Framework reframe 可以 spin 为 \\\"framework reveals that language supervision\\nand action quality are decoupled\\\" 但这是 defensive 而非 proactive contribution。\\n\\n\\n数据已完成：CLIP < DINO in both RSA and R²。VL pretraining 不优于 self-supervised。\\nWorst 档延伸攻击：\\\"CLIP < DINO 说明 language-supervised pretraining 不帮助 action representation。\\n那为什么 VLA 要用 language-supervised encoder（SigLIP）而非 self-supervised（DINO）？更关键的是：\\n如果最好的 action-relevant encoder 不需要 language，你们花整篇论文研究 instruction routing\\n的 practical relevance 在哪里？Instructions 在 VLA 中可能是 overhead 而非 feature。\\n你们应该研究为什么 VLA 不用 DINO 作为 encoder，而非研究 instruction 如何 route through LLM。\\\"\\n这直接挑战论文 premise 而非 findings——worst tier 下论文可能被判 \\\"interesting but\\nfundamentally misdirected\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Branch-split RSA\",\n    \"description\": \"DinoSigLIP fused backbone 中 DINOv2 vs SigLIP branch 分离\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dinov2_branch_rsa\": 0.619,\n      \"siglip_branch_rsa\": 0.621,\n      \"fused_rsa\": 0.634,\n      \"post_projector_rsa\": 0.615\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Architecture-specific detail，appendix material。Framework demo 价值存在但不值得 main text 篇幅。\\n\\n\\n数据不变。DINOv2 ≈ SigLIP in fused backbone（Δ<0.002）。Worst 档下此实验只适用于\\nOpenVLA 的 DinoSigLIP 架构。TracVLA 和 NORA 用完全不同的 vision encoders，\\nbranch-split 不可迁移。Reviewer：\\\"这是 architecture-specific implementation detail，\\n不是 generalizable finding。在 8-page 限制下应移到 appendix。\\\"\\n在 diagnostic framework reframe 下可保留为 \\\"framework 能做 sub-encoder analysis\\\" demo，\\n但 0.5 段就够了。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Architecture R² Exit Collapse Matrix (D096/D099/D102)\",\n    \"description\": \"3 架构 × 4 suite 的 R² exit collapse — D102 VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA 二元分离\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_cells\": 10,\n      \"vlm_to_vla_cells\": 6,\n      \"vlm_to_vla_all_substantial\": true,\n      \"vlm_to_vla_delta_range\": [\n        0.156,\n        0.455\n      ],\n      \"vla_to_vla_cells\": 4,\n      \"vla_to_vla_none_substantial\": true,\n      \"vla_to_vla_delta_range\": [\n        0.033,\n        0.086\n      ],\n      \"nlp_control_delta\": 0.0,\n      \"binary_separation\": \"VLM→VLA 6/6 vs VLA→VLA 0/4\",\n      \"tracvla_goal_delta\": 0.228,\n      \"tracvla_spatial_delta\": 0.138,\n      \"tracvla_object_delta\": 0.294,\n      \"tracvla_long_delta\": 0.198,\n      \"nora_goal_delta\": 0.691,\n      \"nora_spatial_delta\": 0.302,\n      \"openvla_goal_delta\": 0.086,\n      \"openvla_spatial_delta\": 0.037,\n      \"openvla_object_delta\": 0.037,\n      \"openvla_long_delta\": 0.033\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"R² Exit Collapse: D102 Binary Separation (Worst-Tier Reinterpretation)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Transition Type\",\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Suite\",\n          \"Δ (peak-exit)\",\n          \"Worst Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"VLM→VLA\",\n            \"TracVLA (Phi-3→VLA)\",\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"0.228\",\n            \"Expected: domain adaptation reorganization\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLM→VLA\",\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"0.138\",\n            \"Expected: same mechanism\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLM→VLA\",\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Object\",\n            \"0.294\",\n            \"Expected: same mechanism\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLM→VLA\",\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Long\",\n            \"0.198\",\n            \"Expected: same mechanism\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLM→VLA\",\n            \"NORA (Qwen2.5→VLA)\",\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"0.691\",\n            \"Outlier: 3x median, architecture-specific\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLM→VLA\",\n            \"NORA\",\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"0.302\",\n            \"Expected: consistent with NORA pattern\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA→VLA\",\n            \"OpenVLA (OXE→LIBERO)\",\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"0.086\",\n            \"Below threshold: no new collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA→VLA\",\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"0.037\",\n            \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA→VLA\",\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"Object\",\n            \"0.037\",\n            \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA→VLA\",\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"Long\",\n            \"0.033\",\n            \"Below threshold: confirms one-time effect\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Exit Collapse Diagnostic Value Assessment\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Question\",\n          \"Answer\",\n          \"Practical Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Does model show VLM→VLA transition?\",\n            \"Yes, 6/6 cells\",\n            \"Low: practitioner already knows training history\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Can it track ongoing optimization?\",\n            \"No, 0/4 VLA→VLA cells\",\n            \"Zero: one-time marker only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Is magnitude calibrated?\",\n            \"No, 4.4x range within VLM→VLA\",\n            \"Low: cannot compare across architectures\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Does NLP control exclude confound?\",\n            \"Yes, D100 ΔR²=0.000\",\n            \"Defensive win but doesn't add value\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"D102 binary separation 是 scientifically clean 但 worst-tier reviewer 把 clean result\\n重新定义为 trivial result。NLP control 是 necessary defense 但不 sufficient to elevate\\ncontribution。Framework reframe：exit collapse 降为 \\\"one-time transition marker detected\\nby framework\\\" 而非 \\\"architecture-independent routing signature\\\"。价值在 framework 能\\nsystematically detect transition effects 而非 the specific effect detected。\\n\\n\\nD102 更新后数据清晰：VLM→VLA transition 6/6 一致（Δ=0.156-0.455），VLA→VLA 0/4 超过 Δ>0.10\\n阈值（Δ=0.033-0.086）。v3 MCCV 修正了 train-test leakage。D100 NLP control ΔR²=0.000\\n排除了 generic fine-tuning confound。\\n\\n但 worst-tier reviewer 用 D102 的 clean binary 反过来攻击：\\n\\\"你们自己证明了 exit collapse 是 one-time VLM→VLA transition artifact。这很好，但：\\n(1) 这不是 mechanism discovery——当你把 language model 变成 action model，出口层表征\\n当然会重组。任何 domain adaptation（NLP→vision, text→audio）都可能产生类似 transition effects。\\n你排除了 NLP finetuning，但没排除其他 domain adaptation scenarios（e.g., LLM→code generation）。\\n(2) 作为 diagnostic tool 的价值有限：exit collapse 只告诉你 'this model was once a VLM\\nthat got converted to VLA'——但在实践中你已经知道这一点（你知道模型的 training pipeline）。\\n什么时候 practitioner 需要一个 tool 来判断 '我的模型是不是 VLA'？\\n(3) VLA→VLA finetuning 无 exit collapse（0/4）说明它不是 ongoing routing optimization 的\\nindicator——它只是 initial adaptation 的 one-time marker。一个只出现一次的 diagnostic \\n不能用于 iterative VLA development。\\n(4) Magnitude 仍然高度 variable（0.156-0.691, 4.4x range even within VLM→VLA cells），\\nNORA 的 0.691 是 outlier（3x median）。Architecture-independent 的 direction 但\\narchitecture-dependent 的 magnitude——这降低了作为 quantitative diagnostic 的 precision。\\\"\\n\\nD100 NLP control 是 good defense 但不足以救 worst tier——因为 reviewer 的攻击不是\\n\\\"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning\\\" 而是 \\\"exit collapse is trivially expected VLM→VLA transition\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Architecture L1 Attention (D090 Base-Model vs Training)\",\n    \"description\": \"3 架构 L1 instruction-dominant heads — D090 证明 base-model-dependent\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_trained\": 23,\n      \"openvla_oxe_untrained\": 26,\n      \"tracvla_trained\": [\n        27,\n        30\n      ],\n      \"tracvla_untrained_vlm\": 32,\n      \"nora_trained\": [\n        12,\n        13\n      ],\n      \"nora_untrained_vlm\": [\n        13,\n        14\n      ],\n      \"training_effect_on_l1\": \"none or negative\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"L1 Heads: Training Contributes Nothing (D090 Worst Reading)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Base Model\",\n          \"Trained\",\n          \"Untrained\",\n          \"Training Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"Llama-2-7B\",\n            \"24/32\",\n            \"0/32 (random init)\",\n            \"Artifact: random has no LM\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"OXE-pretrained\",\n            \"24/32\",\n            \"25/32 (OXE)\",\n            \"-1: OXE already saturated\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Phi-3-mini\",\n            \"27-30/32\",\n            \"32/32 (VLM base)\",\n            \"-2 to -5: training REDUCES\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NORA\",\n            \"Qwen2.5-VL-3B\",\n            \"12-13/16\",\n            \"13-14/16\",\n            \"-1: no training effect\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Contribution Audit After D090\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Originally Claimed\",\n          \"Post-D090 Status\",\n          \"Remaining Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"L1 routing gradient (0→9→24)\",\n            \"REMOVED: base-model artifact\",\n            \"Zero\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Bookend attention pattern\",\n            \"WEAKENED: entry from base model\",\n            \"Exit engagement only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"R² exit collapse\",\n            \"Retained: training-induced\",\n            \"Thin — one-time transition\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CF sensitivity\",\n            \"Retained: training-induced\",\n            \"Thin — unfair baselines\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Experimental framework\",\n            \"Intact\",\n            \"Main surviving contribution\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"D090 是论文最大的 self-inflicted wound。Framework reframe 试图把 D090 从 weakness 转为\\n\\\"framework's key capability: distinguishing training-induced from pre-existing\\\"——\\n但 reviewer 可能看穿这个 rhetorical move。核心问题：能区分 training vs pretraining\\neffects 是 methodology 贡献，但 CoRL 评审 findings 而非 methods。\\n\\n\\nD090 发现 L1 head count 是 base-model-dependent。Worst tier 核心攻击：\\n\\\"L1 routing gradient（0→9→24 heads）是论文最 visually striking 的结果，但你们自己证明了\\n它不是训练学到的。TracVLA untrained（纯 VLM）已 32/32，训练反而减少到 27-30（repurposing）。\\nNORA untrained 已 13-14/16，训练无变化。OpenVLA 的 0→24 gradient 只是 random init vs\\npretrained 的差异——任何 pretrained LLM 都有 instruction attention heads，不需要 VLA training。\\n\\n这意味着论文最核心的 visual result（Figure X 的 attention head gradient）不能 claim\\n是 VLA training 的贡献。读者看到这个图会以为训练创造了 routing——但实际上 routing 来自\\nlanguage pretraining。这是 misleading framing，即使你在正文中有 caveat。\\\"\\n\\nD090 后 remaining training-induced effects 只剩 exit collapse 和 CF sensitivity。\\nReviewer 总结：\\\"After D090, VLA training's unique contribution is one transition artifact\\n(exit collapse) and one baseline-confounded sensitivity measure (CF). This is too thin\\nfor a full paper at a top robotics venue.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Architecture Counterfactual Sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"3 架构 CF sensitivity — trained vs untrained 对比\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"openvla_goal_trained_d\": 1.182,\n      \"openvla_goal_untrained_d\": 1.048,\n      \"openvla_spatial_trained_d\": 1.173,\n      \"openvla_spatial_untrained_d\": 0.936,\n      \"tracvla_goal_trained_d\": 1.524,\n      \"tracvla_goal_untrained_cos\": 0.153,\n      \"nora_goal_trained_cos\": 1.0,\n      \"nora_goal_untrained_cos\": 0.081,\n      \"incommensurable_pairs\": 5,\n      \"fair_comparison_pairs\": 2,\n      \"openvla_goal_fair_delta\": 0.134,\n      \"openvla_spatial_fair_delta\": 0.237\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"CF Sensitivity: Incommensurability Problem\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Architecture\",\n          \"Suite\",\n          \"Trained Metric\",\n          \"Untrained Metric\",\n          \"Comparable?\",\n          \"Fair Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"d=1.182\",\n            \"d=1.048\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"+0.134 (12%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"OpenVLA\",\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"d=1.173\",\n            \"d=0.936\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"+0.237 (25%)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"d=1.524\",\n            \"cos=0.153\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Incommensurable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Spatial\",\n            \"d=1.333\",\n            \"cos=0.180\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Incommensurable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Object\",\n            \"d=1.212\",\n            \"cos=0.185\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Incommensurable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TracVLA\",\n            \"Long\",\n            \"d=1.473\",\n            \"cos=0.173\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Incommensurable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"NORA\",\n            \"Goal\",\n            \"cos=1.0 (sat.)\",\n            \"cos=0.081\",\n            \"Partially\",\n            \"Saturated — ceiling artifact?\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"CF Sensitivity: Missing Behavioral Validation\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"What CF Shows\",\n          \"What Reviewer Wants\",\n          \"Gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Output direction changes (d>0.5)\",\n            \"Task success rate drops\",\n            \"No closed-loop data\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Empty > wrong > shuffled > para\",\n            \"Perturbation severity → failure rate correlation\",\n            \"No behavioral grounding\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth\",\n            \"Action quality under perturbation\",\n            \"MSE≈0 suggests no quality impact\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CF sensitivity 在 worst tier 下被 double-attacked: incommensurable metrics + no behavioral\\ngrounding。ΔMSE≈0 (ground-truth error unchanged under ablation) is particularly damaging——\\nit suggests CF perturbation changes output direction without degrading quality，\\nsupporting \\\"information-computation dissociation\\\" (Hewitt & Liang 2019) interpretation\\nthat routing modulates output but doesn't encode task-critical information。\\nFramework reframe：CF analysis 降为 \\\"framework's perturbation analysis capability\\\"，\\nbehavioral validation 列为 \\\"critical future work\\\"。\\n\\n\\nD097/D099 修正后，CF sensitivity 的 cross-architecture 对比面临 incommensurability 问题：\\nTracVLA/NORA untrained 无法生成 actions（cosine in hidden space），trained 用 Cohen's d\\nin action space——两个 metrics 不可直接比较。只有 OpenVLA 的 trained + untrained 都能生成\\nactions，可用同一 metric 比较。\\n\\nWorst-tier reviewer 攻击：\\n\\\"CF sensitivity 是你们仅存的两个 training-induced effects 之一（D090 后），但：\\n(1) 你们自己承认 5/7 cross-architecture comparisons 使用 incommensurable metrics（Cohen's d\\nvs cosine distance）。你不能 claim 'training amplifies CF sensitivity' 如果 trained 和\\nuntrained 用不同 metrics 测量——这不是 methodological nuance，这是 fundamental flaw。\\n(2) 唯一公平对比（OpenVLA Goal/Spatial）显示 Δ=+0.13/+0.24，即 trained 比 untrained\\n高 12%/25%。但 OpenVLA untrained 是 OXE-pretrained VLA（已有 strong CF d=1.048），\\n所以 'training amplification' 是 VLA→VLA marginal improvement 而非 VLM→VLA dramatic change。\\n(3) 'Empty instruction produces largest deviation' 在 6/8 settings——这不需要 VLA-specific\\nrouting 来解释。任何 conditioned generative model 在 input 被完全移除时 output 会 change most。\\n这是 conditioning 的 definition 而非 routing mechanism。\\n(4) CF sensitivity 没有 behavioral grounding：output changes（d=0.65-1.5）是否\\n导致 task failure？如果 perturbed instructions 产生 different but equally valid actions，\\nCF sensitivity 不是 routing evidence 而是 representational noise。\\n缺少 behavioral validation（closed-loop success rate under perturbation）是 near-fatal\\nfor CoRL submission。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)\",\n    \"description\": \"VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA → task-finetuned VLA 三层级路由梯度\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tier1_models\": [\n        \"Phi-3-Vision\",\n        \"Qwen2.5-VL\",\n        \"random init Llama-2\"\n      ],\n      \"tier1_l1_heads\": [\n        32,\n        14,\n        0\n      ],\n      \"tier1_cf_max_cos\": 0.19,\n      \"tier1_exit_collapse\": false,\n      \"tier2_model\": \"openvla-7b (OXE)\",\n      \"tier2_l1_heads\": 25,\n      \"tier2_cf_d\": 1.048,\n      \"tier2_exit_collapse\": false,\n      \"tier3_l1_heads\": [\n        24,\n        30,\n        13\n      ],\n      \"tier3_exit_collapse_vlm_origin\": true,\n      \"tier3_exit_collapse_vla_origin\": false,\n      \"tier2_n_datapoints\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Three-Tier Gradient: N=1 at Tier-2\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Tier\",\n          \"N Models\",\n          \"Key Metrics\",\n          \"Worst Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Tier 1 (VLM)\",\n            \"3+\",\n            \"L1: 0-32; CF<0.2; no collapse\",\n            \"Adequate N but heterogeneous (0 vs 32 heads)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Tier 2 (General VLA)\",\n            \"1 ONLY\",\n            \"L1: 25; CF d=1.05; no collapse\",\n            \"N=1 — cannot establish gradient\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Tier 3 (Task VLA)\",\n            \"~10 cells\",\n            \"L1: 13-30; CF d>0.45; collapse if VLM-origin\",\n            \"Adequate N but split by origin\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Three-tier gradient 必须移除或降为 \\\"preliminary observation with N=1 at intermediate tier\\\"。\\nFramework reframe：不 claim gradient，改为 \\\"framework enables stage-wise comparison\\\"——\\ncontribute methodology for comparing training stages, not the gradient finding itself.\\n\\n\\n三层级梯度被 worst reviewer 驳为 post-hoc narrative with N=1 at Tier-2。\\n\\n攻击 1 — 统计力不足：\\\"Tier-2 只有一个数据点（openvla-7b OXE pretrained）。要建立 gradient\\n你需要 at minimum 3 个独立的 OXE-pretrained 或 general-pretrained VLA checkpoints 来\\n验证 Tier-2 不是 openvla-7b specific。Three points don't make a gradient if the middle\\none is N=1——那是 step function with one interpolation point。\\\"\\n\\n攻击 2 — L1 heads 在 tiers 间不单调：\\\"Tier-1 Phi-3-Vision = 32/32, Tier-2 OXE = 25/32,\\nTier-3 TracVLA = 27-30/32。Tier-1 > Tier-2 ≈ Tier-3——这不是 gradient，这是 'base model\\nalready saturated then training reduces some heads'。L1 head count 不支持 gradient narrative。\\\"\\n\\n攻击 3 — Exit collapse 不支持 gradient：\\\"Tier-2 无 exit collapse, Tier-3 有 exit collapse\\n只在 VLM→VLA origin models——这是 binary transition 不是 gradient。如果 Tier-3 只在\\nVLM-origin 有 collapse 而 VLA-origin 没有，那 'gradient' 应该有 collapse 强度在 Tier-2→Tier-3\\nincreasing——但 Tier-2 = 0, Tier-3 (VLA origin) = 0。只有 Tier-3 (VLM origin) 有 collapse。\\n这是 binary (VLM→VLA collapse exists / doesn't) 不是 three-tier gradient。\\\"\\n\\n攻击 4 — libero_finetuned attention data 反驳 gradient：\\\"L31 exit engagement 从 bridge-VLA\\n(18 heads) 到 libero-finetuned (0 heads)——further specialization REDUCES exit routing。\\nGradient predicts 'more training = more routing' 但 data shows opposite at exit layer。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"NLP Finetuning Control (D100)\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-2-7b-chat R² profile 排除 generic fine-tuning confound\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"peak_r2\": 0.1555,\n      \"exit_r2\": 0.1555,\n      \"delta_r2\": 0.0,\n      \"profile_shape\": \"flat constant across all 32 layers\",\n      \"r2_range\": [\n        0.1547,\n        0.1555\n      ],\n      \"phi3_nlp_delta\": 0.0,\n      \"qwen_nlp_delta\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"NLP Finetuning Control Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"Backbone\",\n          \"ΔR²\",\n          \"Profile\",\n          \"Worst Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Llama-2-7b-chat\",\n            \"Llama-2-7B\",\n            \"0.000\",\n            \"Flat 0.155\",\n            \"Expected: no action info anywhere\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Phi-3-mini-instruct\",\n            \"Phi-3-mini\",\n            \"0.000\",\n            \"Flat 0.155\",\n            \"Expected: same noise floor\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-3B-instruct\",\n            \"Qwen2.5-3B\",\n            \"0.000\",\n            \"Flat 0.155\",\n            \"Expected: same noise floor\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLM→VLA (TracVLA)\",\n            \"Phi-3-mini\",\n            \"0.156-0.294\",\n            \"Exit collapse\",\n            \"VLA-specific but trivially expected\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA→VLA (OpenVLA)\",\n            \"Llama-2-7B\",\n            \"0.033-0.086\",\n            \"Mild decline\",\n            \"No new collapse in VLA→VLA\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"D100 是 necessary but not sufficient defense。Worst reviewer accepts the control\\nbut doesn't give credit for it — \\\"excluding an obvious confound is minimum bar,\\nnot contribution.\\\" Framework reframe 可以 cite D100 作为 \\\"framework enables\\ncross-domain comparison\\\" demo，但 reviewer 的 next-level attack（trivially expected）\\n仍 stands。\\n\\n\\nD100 结果 clean：三个 NLP-finetuned LLM（Llama-2-chat, Phi-3-instruct, Qwen2.5-instruct）\\n均 ΔR²=0.000，flat R²≈0.155 noise floor。这排除了 \\\"exit collapse is generic fine-tuning artifact\\\"。\\n\\n但 worst-tier reviewer 不被 impressed：\\n\\\"D100 是 good negative control，我们接受 exit collapse 不是 generic fine-tuning。\\n但这不能 elevate exit collapse 为 interesting finding——它只从 'might be generic artifact'\\n升级为 'VLA-specific but trivially expected'。当你训练一个 language model 来 predict\\n7-DOF robot actions，exit layer 表征当然会被 action training reshape。\\nR²≈0.155 in NLP models 只是说明 NLP models 没有 action-relevant information 在任何层\\n（Ridge 只拟合 between-task variance）——当然不会有 exit collapse。\\n你排除了一个 straw-man confound 但没有建立 positive value。\\nA good control experiment answers 'is this finding real?' — yours answers 'is this finding\\neven more trivially explainable than I thought?'  答案是 No，但 the finding is still trivial。\\\"\\n\\nR²=0.155 本身是 between-task variance baseline（10 tasks → Ridge 可拟合 task identity → \\n0.155 R² from 10-way between-task variance alone）——这是 expected 而非 surprising。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cross-Instruction Classification (C1 Framework)\",\n    \"description\": \"10-way instruction classification 跨层 × 跨条件 — C1 框架核心实验\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"trained_L1_acc\": 0.996,\n      \"trained_L2_to_L31\": 1.0,\n      \"llama2base_L1_acc\": 0.802,\n      \"llama2base_L5_plus\": 1.0,\n      \"untrained_L1_acc\": 1.0,\n      \"untrained_L31_acc\": 0.82,\n      \"image_mean_all_layers\": 0.1,\n      \"loocv_trained\": \"100.00±0.00\",\n      \"loocv_untrained\": \"84.76±11.59\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Instruction Classification: Trivially Easy?\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"L1 Acc\",\n          \"L31 Acc\",\n          \"Worst Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Trained\",\n            \"99.6%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"Flat 100% = ceiling effect, no gradient to analyze\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Llama-2 base\",\n            \"80.2%\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"LM pretraining provides separability, not VLA training\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Untrained (random)\",\n            \"100%\",\n            \"82%\",\n            \"Even random features separate 10 classes at L1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Image mean\",\n            \"10%\",\n            \"10%\",\n            \"Causal mask guarantee, not finding\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C1 的 experimental framework 是 reframe 后的 primary contribution。但 cross-instruction\\nclassification 作为 framework demo 的问题：10-way on 4096d 太 easy，不 demonstrate\\nframework 在 harder settings 下的 value。需要更 challenging classification tasks\\n或 fine-grained metrics 来 justify framework utility。\\n\\n\\n数据完整。Worst 档下 C1 被彻底降级：\\n\\\"10-way classification on 4096-dim features 是 trivially easy。Untrained (random init)\\nL1 也达到 100%——random projection 就能分离 10 个 class。你的 LOOCV 只在 untrained deep layers\\n下降到 85%——这不是 'training improves routing' 而是 'random weights corrupt signal in deep layers'。\\n\\nImage mean = 10% at all layers 是 causal mask guarantee 不是 finding。你自己承认了。\\n\\n三条件对比（trained flat 100%, llama2base saturates L5, untrained decays to 82%）的\\ninterpretation 也被质疑：'trained L1=99.6% vs llama2base L1=80.2%' 看起来像 'training\\ncreates immediate routing'，但 D090 证明 L1 heads 来自 base model 而非 training。\\n那 99.6% vs 80.2% 的差异可能只反映 VLA fine-tuning 后 feature quality 提升（action-relevant\\nfeatures are more linearly separable）而非 routing reorganization。\\n\\n贡献在 methodology（factorial design + 4 methods）而非 findings。但 methodology 贡献在\\nCoRL 通常只值 weak accept——CoRL 偏好 systems + behavioral results。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Head Ablation and Specificity Controls\",\n    \"description\": \"L1 attention head ablation 实验套件 — 验证 instruction-dominant heads 的功能特异性\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_r2_L13\": 0.676,\n      \"ablate_24_instr_r2_L13\": 0.676,\n      \"ablate_24_random_r2_L13\": 0.664,\n      \"random_24_z_score\": -2.73,\n      \"specificity_ratio\": 1.08,\n      \"instruction_d\": 0.651,\n      \"random_24_d\": 0.601,\n      \"image_24_d\": 0.58,\n      \"gt_error_delta_mse\": -0.001\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Head Ablation: No Functional Specificity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Ablation Group\",\n          \"24h d\",\n          \"Per-head d\",\n          \"GT ΔMSE\",\n          \"Worst Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Instr-dominant 24\",\n            \"0.651\",\n            \"0.027\",\n            \"-0.001 (p=0.52)\",\n            \"Changes direction, not quality\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random 24 (avg)\",\n            \"0.601\",\n            \"0.025\",\n            \"similar\",\n            \"Any 24 heads produce similar effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Image-dominant 24\",\n            \"0.580\",\n            \"0.024\",\n            \"similar\",\n            \"No group specificity\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Control 8 (random)\",\n            \"0.410\",\n            \"0.051\",\n            \"similar\",\n            \"Per-head effect LARGER in control\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Head ablation suite is worst tier's most damaging evidence against CF sensitivity as\\nfunctional routing. ΔMSE≈0 + specificity ratio 1.08x together argue that instruction\\nrouting (as measured by attention head dominance) has no disproportionate functional role.\\nFramework reframe 很难 rescue this——the framework's own ablation tool reveals that\\nthe effect it detected (instruction routing) is not functionally specific.\\n\\n\\n数据已完成。Worst 档下 ablation 结果被严厉解读：\\n\\n(1) Specificity ratio = 1.08x 极弱：\\\"instruction-dominant 24 heads 的 per-head effect\\n不比 random 24 heads 大多少（z=-2.73 但 effect size tiny）。任何 24/32 heads ablation\\n产生 similar or larger R² increase（random 24 mean delta = 0.077 > instruction 24 delta = 0.042）。\\nInstruction-dominant heads 不是 special——they're 75% of all heads，removing ANY 75%\\nof heads produces similar effects。\\\"\\n\\n(2) ΔMSE≈0 vs ground-truth 是 worst tier 最致命的 finding：\\\"你 ablate 24 instruction-dominant\\nheads，action outputs change direction (d=0.65) 但 ground-truth error 不变（ΔMSE=-0.001, p=0.52）。\\n这意味着 instruction routing 对 action quality 无影响——perturbation 改变 output 方向\\n但不改变 output 质量。这直接证明 CF sensitivity 缺乏 functional significance。\\n如果移除 75% 的 'instruction routing heads' 对 action quality 无影响，\\n那 instruction routing 在 action generation 中可能是 redundant mechanism。\\\"\\n\\n(3) Information-computation dissociation 解读在 worst tier 下被反转：论文 cite Hewitt & Liang 2019\\n作为 \\\"ΔMSE≈0 is expected under dissociation\\\"，但 reviewer 说：\\n\\\"Hewitt & Liang 的 point 是 probe results don't prove representation is functionally used。\\n你在用他们的 framework 来 excuse 你的 negative result。ΔMSE≈0 doesn't support 'routing\\nmodulates without degrading'——it supports 'routing doesn't matter for output quality'。\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Counterfactual Token Overlap and Trajectory-Level Analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"CF perturbation 的 token overlap, trajectory-level d, 和 ΔMSE 扩展分析\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"token_overlap_spearman\": 1.0,\n      \"empty_d_token\": 0.968,\n      \"empty_d_trajectory\": 3.438,\n      \"wrong_d_token\": 0.844,\n      \"wrong_d_trajectory\": 3.798,\n      \"shuffled_d_token\": 0.625,\n      \"shuffled_d_trajectory\": 2.595,\n      \"para_d_token\": 0.697,\n      \"para_d_trajectory\": 2.131,\n      \"inflation_factor_mean\": 0.245,\n      \"gt_mse_original\": 0.498,\n      \"gt_mse_top24_ablated\": 0.497,\n      \"gt_mse_delta\": -0.001\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Token Overlap → Cohen's d: Surface-Level Sensitivity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Perturbation\",\n          \"Token Novelty\",\n          \"Token d\",\n          \"Traj d\",\n          \"Worst Reading\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"empty\",\n            \"1.0\",\n            \"0.968\",\n            \"3.438\",\n            \"Max novelty → max effect: lexical, not semantic\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"wrong\",\n            \"0.83\",\n            \"0.844\",\n            \"3.798\",\n            \"High novelty → high effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"paraphrased\",\n            \"0.47\",\n            \"0.697\",\n            \"2.131\",\n            \"Low novelty → low effect\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"shuffled\",\n            \"0.0\",\n            \"0.625\",\n            \"2.595\",\n            \"Zero novelty but positional change → moderate\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ρ=1.0 token-novelty/d correlation is worst-tier's strongest argument that CF sensitivity\\nmeasures lexical sensitivity rather than semantic routing. Framework reframe has no good\\ncounter — the framework's own analysis reveals CF is surface-level. Could argue \\\"shuffled\\nsame tokens different order still produces d=0.63\\\" as evidence of positional sensitivity\\nbeyond pure lexical, but this is weak defense.\\n\\n\\n数据已完成。Worst 档下 token overlap analysis 被反过来用：\\n\\n\\\"Spearman ρ=1.0 between token novelty and Cohen's d 说明 CF sensitivity 完全由\\nlexical/positional distance 驱动，不是 semantic distance。Empty（最大 token novelty）→\\nlargest d，shuffled（same tokens, different order）→ moderate d，paraphrased（high overlap）→\\nsmallest d。这不是 'the model understands instruction semantics'——这是 'the model responds\\nto surface-level token changes'。任何 autoregressive language model 都会如此。\\\"\\n\\nTrajectory-level d（2.1-3.8）远大于 token-level d（0.6-0.97）——inflation factor ~4x。\\nWorst reviewer：\\\"trajectory-level inflation 说明 per-timestep effects 累积——这不是\\n'stronger evidence of routing' 而是 'autocorrelation amplification'。每个 timestep\\n的小 perturbation 通过 temporal autocorrelation 累积成大 trajectory difference，\\n这是 dynamical systems 的 trivial property 不是 routing evidence。\\\"\\n\\nGT MSE unchanged（0.498 vs 0.497）再次确认 CF perturbation 不影响 action quality。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"D090 Synthesis: What VLA Training Actually Contributes\",\n    \"description\": \"综合评估：D090 后论文的 residual contribution\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"training_induced_effects\": [\n        \"R² exit collapse (VLM→VLA only)\",\n        \"CF sensitivity (unfair baselines)\"\n      ],\n      \"base_model_effects\": [\n        \"L1 head count\",\n        \"deep-layer probe stability\"\n      ],\n      \"removed_contributions\": [\n        \"L1 routing gradient\",\n        \"attention bookend pattern (entry component)\"\n      ],\n      \"remaining_unique\": \"1-2 effects, both with caveats\",\n      \"reviewer_avg_score\": [\n        4.0,\n        5.5\n      ],\n      \"strong_reject_count\": [\n        1,\n        2\n      ],\n      \"accept_probability\": [\n        0.05,\n        0.2\n      ],\n      \"claims_surviving\": [\n        0.5,\n        1.5\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Worst-Tier Score Prediction\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Reviewer\",\n          \"Score\",\n          \"Primary Concern\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"R1 (behavioral)\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"No closed-loop validation; CoRL is robotics venue\",\n            \"Reject\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"R2 (methodology)\",\n            \"6\",\n            \"Framework solid; findings thin but honest\",\n            \"Weak Accept\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"R3 (generalizability)\",\n            \"4\",\n            \"Magnitude variance; incommensurable baselines; over-qualified claims\",\n            \"Reject\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean\",\n            \"4.67\",\n            \"2 reject + 1 weak accept\",\n            \"Likely Reject\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Reframe Impact on Scores\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Reframe Element\",\n          \"Score Impact\",\n          \"Which Reviewer\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"C1 framework as primary contribution\",\n            \"+1 for R2 only\",\n            \"R2: 6→7\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"D090 as framework capability demo\",\n            \"+0.5 for R2\",\n            \"R2 already sympathetic\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Exit collapse as diagnostic\",\n            \"0 for R1/R3\",\n            \"Doesn't address behavioral gap\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Roadmap for closed-loop future work\",\n            \"+0.5 for R1 maybe\",\n            \"R1 may soften to 4.5\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Net after reframe\",\n            \"Mean ~5.0\",\n            \"Still borderline reject\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Worst tier 核心判定：论文 honest analysis (D090) + thorough controls (D100) 是 scientifically\\ncommendable 但 strategically devastating。每个 defense 实验排除了一个 confound 但同时削弱了\\ncontribution scope。D090 证明 L1 routing 不是训练效果；D100 证明 exit collapse 不是 generic\\nfinetuning 但仍被视为 trivial；ΔMSE≈0 证明 ablation 不影响 quality 但被解读为 \\\"routing\\ndoesn't functionally matter\\\"。\\n\\nReframe 路径：diagnostic framework + honest empirical characterization。Accept probability\\n0.05-0.20 range。需要 AC 认可 methodology contribution 的 standalone value 才有机会。\\n关键 rebuttal material：(1) representation engineering literature 论证 representational\\nanalysis 的独立价值，(2) exit collapse as VLM→VLA binary diagnostic 的 concrete use case\\n（判断 pretraining checkpoint 是否完成 VLA transition），(3) framework reusability 的\\n具体 demonstration（how others can apply it to new VLAs）。\\n\\nD090 后 contribution audit 在 worst tier 下：\\n\\nTraining-induced（retained but weakened）:\\n- R² exit collapse：6/6 VLM→VLA, 0/4 VLA→VLA — clean binary。D100 排除 NLP confound。\\n  但 worst reviewer 视为 \\\"trivially expected transition artifact\\\"。\\n- CF sensitivity：d≥0.45 in all trained settings。但 incommensurable baselines（5/7 pairs），\\n  ρ=1.0 token-novelty correlation（surface-level），ΔMSE≈0（no functional consequence）。\\n\\nBase-model-dependent（removed from contribution）:\\n- L1 head count：Phi-3 32/32 untrained, NORA 13/16 untrained — not training-induced。\\n- Deep-layer stability：Llama-2 base also stable（100% L5+）— from LM pretraining。\\n\\nReviewer score prediction:\\n- R1（expects behavioral results）：4/10 — \\\"descriptive analysis without actionable insight,\\n  CoRL expects at minimum open-loop policy evaluation.\\\"\\n- R2（appreciates methodology）：6/10 — \\\"framework is solid and systematic, cross-architecture\\n  validation is thorough engineering. But findings are thin after D090 self-critique.\\\"\\n- R3（generalizability focus）：4/10 — \\\"exit collapse magnitude 4.4x range within VLM→VLA,\\n  CF baselines incommensurable. Claims are over-qualified to the point of being unfalsifiable.\\\"\\nMean: 4.67. Strong reject: 0-1. Accept probability: 0.10-0.20.\\n\\nReframe 能做的最大提升：如果 C1 framework 成功 pitch 为 primary contribution（\\\"first\\nsystematic VLA profiling toolkit\\\"），R2 可能升到 7，但 R1/R3 不变——\\n结果 mean 5.0，borderline reject。需要 AC 同情才有机会。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1267,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1267}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A4KsZzv2Az594ZBCuTdS4x","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — vla-ssd (D060 Reframe → D095 Cross-Architecture Upgrade)\n2\t\n3\t> D048: PI 批准按最大质量重构。A+ 版本保留为 fallback (branch paper-a-plus-backup)。\n4\t> D060: Round 4 weak reject → C1 降为框架, C2 升为唯一核心 claim, C3 降为 qualified observation。\n5\t> D088-D094: 跨架构验证完成（OpenVLA/Llama-2, TraceVLA/Phi-3, NORA/Qwen2.5-VL × 4 LIBERO suites）。C2 从单架构观察升级为跨架构 robust finding。RC4 基本解决。\n6\t\n7\t## Target Venue\n8\t- Primary: CoRL 2026\n9\t- Deadline: Abstract May 26, Paper May 29\n10\t- Format: 8 pages + references\n11\t\n12\t## Core Insight\n13\t\n14\tVLA fine-tuning 的核心贡献是学习 deliberate instruction routing——**跨三种 VLA 架构（Llama-2-7B, Phi-3-mini, Qwen2.5-VL-3B）和四种任务类型一致成立**。训练将 instruction 表征从 LLM 预训练的中层处理模式 reorganize 到 entry-exit bookend 模式，同时在出口层制造 R² collapse（action-relevant information 在 exit 层被选择性丢弃）。跨架构一致性表明这是 VLA 训练的 emergent property，而非特定模型的 artifact。\n15\t\n16\t**两类效应区分（D090）**：\n17\t- **Training-induced（architecture-independent）**: R² exit collapse、counterfactual sensitivity 提升 — 三架构一致\n18\t- **Base-model-dependent（NOT training-induced）**: L1 head count — 取决于 base VLM/LLM 的预训练 attention 模式\n19\t\n20\t**三层级路由梯度（D094）**: VLM base（无 routing）→ OXE-pretrained VLA（通用 routing）→ task-finetuned VLA（任务特化 routing）。Routing 在 VLM→VLA 转换时 emerge，在 general→task-specific 转换时 reshape。\n21\t\n22\t## Core Claims (D060 重构：1 核心 + 1 框架 + 1 观察)\n23\t\n24\t### C1: Experimental Framework + Architecture-Verified Specialization [方法论贡献，非 empirical finding]\n25\t**重新定位（D060）**: Token-level specialization 是 causal mask 的数学必然（image tokens 在序列中先于 instruction tokens，无法 attend to instructions）+ frozen encoder 不接收 instruction input。论文贡献不是\"发现\"这一点，而是：\n26\t- **(a) 系统实验框架**：factorial design (trained/pretrained/untrained × instruction presence) + 四种互补分析方法（cross-instruction probe + attention + RSA + MLP probe），适用于任何 decoder-only VLA\n27\t- **(b) 量化验证**：即使 residual stream 理论上可以 leak information，image tokens 在实际模型的全部 32 层均保持 chance（10%）。这不是 trivial——frozen encoder 权重与 LLM 权重共享 residual stream，验证了 no leakage\n28\t- **(c) 训练差异的量化**：untrained readout L1=100% 但 L31=82%（信号衰减）vs trained 100% 全程稳定——framework 揭示了训练影响 routing robustness 而非 routing existence\n29\t\n30\tKey evidence (unchanged):\n31\t- Cross-instruction probe: same frame × 10 instructions → 10-way classification\n32\t- Dense L0-L32: image_mean = chance at ALL layers\n33\t- LOOCV: 100%±0.00 trained, decaying untrained\n34\t- **承认**: 10-way classification 本身 trivially easy（untrained L1 也 100%），贡献在于 framework + 三条件对比揭示的 routing 差异\n35\t\n36\t### C2: Three Qualitatively Different Routing Strategies — VLA Fine-tuning Achieves Immediate Dedicated Routing\n37\t三条件揭示三种定性不同的 routing 模式：\n38\t\n39\t**L1 Attention Routing (heads + attention fraction):**\n40\t- **Untrained (random init)**: 0/32 heads, 12% text attention\n41\t- **Llama-2 base (pretrained, no VLA)**: 9/32 heads, 36.5% text attention\n42\t- **VLA Trained**: 24/32 heads, 58% text attention\n43\t\n44\t**Full-Layer Probe Profile (instruction classification accuracy):**\n45\t- **Trained**: L1=99.6% → 全程 100% — \"即时路由 + 完全稳定\"\n46\t- **Llama-2 base**: L1=80.2% → L2=98.7% → L5+=100% — \"渐进建立 + 稳定维持\"\n47\t- **Untrained**: L1=100% → L8=98.6% → L31=82% — \"偶然路由 + 逐渐遗忘\"\n48\t\n49\t**VLA Fine-tuning 的独特贡献（精��化）：**\n50\t1. **即时性**：L1 即达 99.6%（vs pretrained 需 5 层才饱和）\n51\t2. **头数专用化**：24/32 heads instruction-dominant（vs pretrained 9/32）\n52\t3. **不是**深层稳定性 — 稳定性来自 pretrained weights（pretrained 也不衰减）\n53\t\n54\t**深层���减只发生在 random init**：说明结构化的 pretrained 表示（无论是否经过 VLA 训练）都能维持 instruction signal；random weights 的噪声累积导致信号退化。\n55\t\n56\t**Full 32-Layer Attention Profile（D054 升级，dense evidence）：**\n57\t- **Untrained**: 全 32 层 × 所有 head = 0 instruction-dominant。完全无语言处理能力。\n58\t- **Llama-2 base**: 倒U型 — L0-L4 低(0-10 heads) → L9-L16 高峰(15-22 heads) → L31 回落(8)。经典 LM pattern：中层做深度语义处理。\n59\t- **VLA Trained**: 书挡型 — L0-L1 高峰(21-24 heads) → L2-L30 低谷(0-11) → L31 再次高峰(18)。入口获取 instruction + 出口条件化 action output。\n60\t\n61\t**C2 Claim（D073 reframe: open-loop functional sensitivity）**: VLA fine-tuning **shifts** instruction attention from mid-layer processing (Llama-2 base: 15-22/32 heads at L10-L17) to entry-layer routing (L0-L1: 21-24/32) and exit-layer re-engagement (L31: 18/32)。Instruction-conditioned action generation operates through **distributed L1 routing** where instruction-attention fraction predicts per-head contribution magnitude (specificity ratio 1.08x at action output)。Routing modulates output direction (d=0.65) without systematic quality degradation (ΔMSE≈0), consistent with an information-computation dissociation (Hewitt & Liang 2019)。不能 claim instruction heads \"uniquely responsible\" 或 \"confirms routing function\"——用 \"open-loop functional sensitivity\" + \"support\" 而非 \"confirm\"。可 claim \"disproportionate contribution\" + \"attention-ordered routing\"。Section 标题用 \"Open-loop functional sensitivity\"，正文用 \"shifts...from...to...\" + \"distributed routing\"。\n62\t\n63\tKey evidence:\n64\t- **32-layer dense attention profile**: Trained bookend (L0-1: 21-24, L31: 18) vs Llama2base inverted-U (L9-16: 15-22)\n65\t- Three-condition full-layer probe: trained flat 100%; llama2base saturates L5+100%; untrained decays L1:100%→L31:82%\n66\t- L1 attention gradient: 0/32 → 9/32 → 24/32 heads\n67\t- VLA-specific contributions: (1) temporal reorganization from mid-peak to bookend, (2) immediacy (L1: 80.2→99.6%), (3) head dedication (9→25 at L1)\n68\t- **Per-token normalization**: 38.2x text/image ratio (trained instr-dom) vs 1.5x (untrained) — eliminates token-count confound\n69\t- **Trajectory-level d**: all conditions d>2.0 (token-level is conservative ~4x underestimate)\n70\t- **GT error**: ΔMSE≈0 (ablation redirects outputs without degrading GT accuracy) — supports information-computation dissociation\n71\t- **Token overlap**: Spearman ρ=1.0 between token novelty and d — lexical/positional sensitivity, not semantic distance\n72\t- **LOO sensitivity**: all leave-one-out p ≤ 0.083, no qualitative reversal; cream cheese reclassification p=0.008\n73\t- **4-condition training trajectory (D075)**: untrained(0) → llama2(9) → bridge-vla(24) → libero-finetuned(22) at L1。Entry routing 稳定，但 L31 exit engagement 18→0（entry-exit → entry-only sharpening）。Probe accuracy 不变（L31 仍 100%），确认 attention-representation dissociation\n74\t- **OXE training diversity**: openvla-7b 在 Open X-Embodiment 970K episodes（多平台多任务）上训练，L1 routing 不是 LIBERO-specific\n75\t\n76\t#### C2-X: Cross-Architecture Validation (D088-D094 — 论文最强升级)\n77\t\n78\t**三架构 × 四 suite 矩阵**验证 C2 不是 OpenVLA-specific artifact：\n79\t\n80\t**R² Exit Collapse（D096 修正：VLM→VLA transition effect, NOT universally architecture-independent）：**\n81\t\n82\t| Arch (backbone) | Suite | Trained Δ (peak−exit) | Untrained Δ | Collapse? | Note |\n83\t|-----------------|-------|----------------------|-------------|-----------|------|\n84\t| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Goal | 0.016 | 0.033 | ❌ | untrained(OXE) Δ更大 |\n85\t| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Spatial | 0.037 | TBD | ❌ | v3 MCCV: below Δ>0.10 threshold |\n86\t| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Object | 0.037 | 0.076 | ❌ | v3 MCCV: below Δ>0.10 threshold |\n87\t| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Long (OFT) | 0.004 | 0.016 | ❌ | OFT finetuning, 两条件均平坦 |\n88\t| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Goal | 0.228 | 0.048 | ✅ | |\n89\t| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Spatial | 0.138 | 0.016 | ✅ | |\n90\t| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Object | 0.294 | 0.009 | ✅ | |\n91\t| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Long | 0.198 | 0.028 | ✅ | |\n92\t| NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B) | Goal | 0.691 | 0.044 | ✅ | 最极端 |\n93\t| NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B) | Spatial | 0.302 | 0.037 | ✅ | |\n94\t\n95\t**D096+D099+D102 修正结论（v3 MCCV 更新）**：R² exit collapse 在 VLM→VLA 转换中 6/6 一致（TracVLA + NORA 所有 untrained 均为纯 VLM，Δ=0.156-0.455）。在 OXE-pretrained→LIBERO 转换中 0/4 cells 超过 Δ>0.10 阈值（Goal Δ=0.086, Spatial Δ=0.037, Object Δ=0.037, Long Δ=0.033）。v3 demo-level MCCV 修正了 v2 的 train-test leakage 后，OpenVLA Spatial/Object 的 Δ 从 0.110/0.121 下降至 0.037/0.037，证实 VLA→VLA 转换不产生实质性 exit collapse。\n96\t\n97\t**解读（D102 更新）**：Exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA 转换的 one-time reorganization effect (6/6)，在 VLA→VLA (OXE→LIBERO) 进一步 finetuning 中不再重现 (0/4)。这一二元分离比之前的 \"task-dependent\" 解读更清晰——区分因素是 transition type（VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA），而非 task difficulty。\n98\t\n99\t**论文写法**：改为 \"R² exit collapse consistently emerges when VLMs are first fine-tuned into VLAs (6/6 cells across two architectures, Δ = 0.156–0.455). In contrast, when an already-pretrained VLA undergoes further task-specific fine-tuning, no cell exceeds the Δ > 0.10 threshold (0/4 OpenVLA cells, Δ = 0.033–0.086), indicating that exit collapse is a one-time reorganization associated with the VLM-to-VLA transition rather than a cumulative effect of continued training.\"\n100\t\n101\t**D100 NLP Finetuning Control — Exit Collapse 是 VLA-Specific**：\n102\tLlama-2-7b-chat（同 Llama-2-7B backbone，SFT+RLHF fine-tuned）R² per-layer 全层平坦（0.1547-0.1555），Δ=0.000。对比同 backbone 的 VLM→VLA 转换：TracVLA Δ=0.156-0.294, NORA Δ=0.302-0.455。OpenVLA (VLA→VLA) Δ=0.033-0.086 同样无实质性 collapse，进一步确认 exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA 转换特有现象。\n103\t\n104\t**意义**：控制了架构（同 Llama-2-7B）和 fine-tuning（NLP chat 也是 fine-tuned model）两个变量后，exit collapse 仅在 VLM→VLA 转换中出现（Δ=0.156-0.455），NLP finetuning (Δ=0.000) 和 VLA→VLA finetuning (Δ=0.033-0.086) 均无。这排除了 \"exit collapse is a generic fine-tuning artifact\" 的解释，确认 exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA transition-specific 的表征重组。R² ≈ 0.155 是 noise floor（NLP 模型无 action representation，Ridge 仅拟合 between-task variance）。\n105\t\n106\t**论文写法**：在 exit collapse 结论后加 \"A chat-finetuned control sharing the same Llama-2-7B backbone exhibits flat R² ≈ 0.16 across all layers (Δ ≈ 0), confirming that exit collapse is specific to action-oriented training rather than an inherent consequence of transformer fine-tuning.\"\n107\t\n108\t**L1 Instruction-Dominant Heads（D090: base-model-dependent, NOT training-induced）：**\n109\t\n110\t| Arch | Suite | Trained | Untrained | 解读 |\n111\t|------|-------|---------|-----------|------|\n112\t| OpenVLA | Goal | 23/32 | 26/32 (OXE pretrained) | Finetuning 减少 3 头（→mixed），h13 跨条件共有 |\n113\t| OpenVLA | Object | 24/32 | 24/32 (OXE pretrained) | OXE 已创建 routing |\n114\t| OpenVLA | Long | 14/32 (OFT) | 25/32 (OXE) | OFT 增加 mixed heads |\n115\t| TracVLA | All 4 suites | 27-30/32 | 32/32 | Phi-3-Vision 预训练已 32/32 全极化 |\n116\t| NORA | Goal | 13/16 | 13/16 | Qwen2.5-VL 预训练已 13/16 |\n117\t| NORA | Spatial | 12/16 | 14/16 | 同上 |\n118\t\n119\t**关键区分**: L1 head count 反映 base model 的语言预训练 attention 模式，**不是** VLA 训练效果。TracVLA untrained（纯 VLM）已 32/32，训练反而减少到 27-30/32（repurpose some heads）。**论文不能 claim L1 heads 是训练学到的**——只能 claim R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 是训练效果。\n120\t\n121\t**Counterfactual Sensitivity（training-induced）：**\n122\t\n123\t| Arch | Suite | Trained (top d/cos) | Untrained (top d/cos) | 训练效应 |\n124\t|------|-------|---------------------|----------------------|----------|\n125\t| OpenVLA | Goal | d=1.18 (wrong) | d=1.05 (empty) | ✓ same metric, Δ=+0.13; wrong>empty (1.182>1.170) |\n126\t| OpenVLA | Spatial | d=1.17 (empty) | d=0.94 (empty) | ✓ same metric, Δ=+0.23 |\n127\t| OpenVLA | Object | d=1.21 (empty) | cos=0.569 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n128\t| TracVLA | Goal | d=1.52 (empty) | cos=0.153 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n129\t| TracVLA | Spatial | d=1.33 (empty) | cos=0.180 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n130\t| TracVLA | Object | d=1.21 (empty) | cos=0.185 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n131\t| TracVLA | Long | d=1.47 (empty) | cos=0.173 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n132\t| NORA | Goal | cos=1.0 (saturated) | cos=0.081 | ✓ same metric, 12× |\n133\t\n134\t**D097+D099 修正**: TracVLA/NORA 的 trained 用 Cohen's d（action space），untrained 用 cosine distance（hidden space），两者不可比。但 OpenVLA 的 trained + untrained 均可生成 actions，可用同一 metric (Cohen's d) 公平比较。结果：trained 全面高于 untrained 但 gap 适中（Goal Δ=+0.04, Spatial Δ=+0.24），因为 OpenVLA untrained (OXE pretrained) 已是训练过的 VLA。这是唯一可做公平 trained-untrained 对比的架构。\n135\t\n136\t\"empty\" 在 6/8 tested trained settings 排第一（exceptions: OpenVLA Goal \"wrong\" first 1.182>1.170; OpenVLA Long \"shuffled\" first 0.565>0.505）。OpenVLA Long 整体 d 偏低（0.45-0.57），与 OFT finetuning 相关。\n137\t\n138\t**TracVLA Universal Mixed Heads (D091)**: h13 和 h22 在全部 4 个 LIBERO suite 的 trained 模型中一致作为 \"mixed\" head 出现（非 instruction-dominant 也非 image-dominant），而 untrained (Phi-3-Vision) 无此 pattern。暗示训练创建了功能特化的 mixed-modality heads。\n139\t\n140\t**Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)**:\n141\t- **Tier 1 — VLM base (无 action training)**: TracVLA untrained (Phi-3-Vision) / NORA untrained (Qwen2.5-VL) — 无 R² collapse，无 CF sensitivity（cos < 0.2），L1 heads 来自语言预训练\n142\t- **Tier 2 — OXE-pretrained VLA (通用 action training)**: OpenVLA untrained (openvla-7b, 970K OXE episodes) — 已有强 L1 routing (25/32)，强 CF (d=1.048)，无 exit collapse\n143\t- **Tier 3 — Task-finetuned VLA**: TracVLA/NORA trained — R² exit collapse (Δ=0.156-0.455) + task-specific CF pattern。OpenVLA trained (VLA→VLA) 无额外 exit collapse (Δ=0.033-0.086)，但有 CF sharpening\n144\t\n145\t**论文 story 升级**: 从 \"VLA training creates routing\" 升级为 \"routing emerges at VLM→VLA transition and reshapes at general→task-specific transition\"。\n146\t\n147\t### C3: Vision Encoder Geometry Observation [降为 qualified observation，非 core claim]\n148\t**重新定位（D060）**: RSA inverted-U 的 rise phase 极小（Δρ=0.016, CI 待补），CKA 完全反转 RSA ordering（untrained > trained > DINOv2），\"non-monotonic refinement\" 仅在 RSA 下成立。DINOv2 ranking 在 CKA 下不成立（CKA 中 DINOv2 排名最低）。\n149\t\n150\t**保留为 observation 的理由**：\n151\t- **Decline phase 也是 RSA-specific**：L12→L32 Δρ=-0.206 远大于 rise phase，但 CKA 单调递增无 decline。不能 claim decline 是 metric-robust。\n152\t- **R² inverted-U 是 metric-independent 的**：functional probe 确认 L8-L13 peak（0.655-0.678），之后下降。这是 C3 最强的 evidence，不依赖 RSA/CKA 选择。\n153\t- **Metric divergence 本身是 honest observation**：\"non-monotonic under RSA, monotonic under CKA\"\n154\t- **DINOv2 RSA ranking**：在 RSA 下 robust，但必须加 \"under RSA\" qualifier\n155\t\n156\t**写法要求**：\n157\t- Abstract/Intro 中\"non-monotonic refinement\"加 \"under RSA\" qualifier\n158\t- DINOv2 \"highest geometric foundation\" 加 \"as measured by RSA\"\n159\t- best-vs-best Δ=+0.017 明确标 n.s.（CI includes 0）\n160\t- Discussion 加 metric-dependence caveat（CKA 反转在正文中 qualify，不只在 appendix）\n161\t\n162\tKey evidence (unchanged but qualified):\n163\t- Cross-encoder RSA table — **加 \"under RSA\" qualifier**\n164\t- Per-layer RSA + R² profiles — **rise phase CI 待补报**\n165\t- Cross-benchmark replication — still holds\n166\t- **CKA divergence** — 必须在正文 acknowledge\n167\t\n168\t## Story Spine (D095 Cross-Architecture Upgrade)\n169\t\n170\t- **Problem**: VLAs fine-tune LLMs on robot data, but how training reshapes instruction routing and information integration at the token level remains uncharacterized — and whether these effects generalize across architectures is unknown.\n171\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Prior behavioral studies (Grant et al. 2026, Haon et al. 2025) found visual dominance and instruction underutilization, but did not decompose the representational roles of different token positions, explain how training reshapes information flow, or test generalization across VLA families.\n172\t- **Our framing**: We provide a systematic experimental framework for token-level analysis of VLAs, validated across three architectures (Llama-2-7B, Phi-3-mini, Qwen2.5-VL-3B) and four task suites. We find two consistent cross-architecture training effects: (1) trained VLAs exhibit substantial counterfactual sensitivity to instruction perturbation (Cohen's d ≥ 0.45), though metric incomparability with untrained baselines precludes quantifying the amplification; (2) R² exit collapse emerges consistently when VLMs are first fine-tuned into VLAs (6/6 cells, Δ=0.156-0.455), but does not appear in VLA-to-VLA fine-tuning (0/4 cells, Δ=0.033-0.086). A three-tier routing gradient (VLM base → general VLA → task-specific VLA) reveals that routing reorganization is a staged process.\n173\t- **Headline results**: (1) [Framework] Systematic token-level analysis framework applicable to any decoder-only VLA, validated on 3 architectures × 4 task suites (10 cells). (2) [Core finding — CF sensitivity] Counterfactual sensitivity consistently present in trained VLAs (Cohen's d ≥ 0.45 across two architectures and eight suite combinations); metric incomparability between trained (action MSE) and untrained (cosine distance) conditions precludes quantifying the gap as a single ratio. (3) [Core finding — R² exit collapse] Collapse emerges at VLM→VLA transition (6/6 TracVLA+NORA cells, Δ=0.156-0.455) but not at VLA→VLA transition (0/4 OpenVLA cells, Δ=0.033-0.086) — one-time reorganization at VLM→VLA boundary. (4) [Core finding — routing gradient] Three-tier gradient: VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA (general routing) → task-finetuned (task-specific, with CF sharpening). (5) [Nuance — D090] L1 head count is base-model-dependent (Phi-3 32/32 both conditions), not training-induced. (6) [Observation] Under RSA, vision encoder geometry follows inverted-U; functional probes confirm L8-L13 peak.\n174\t- **Practical implications**: (1) VLA architecture design should optimize entry-exit instruction routing. (2) R² exit collapse is a diagnostic signature of initial VLA training — its presence/absence reveals the pretraining stage. (3) The routing gradient suggests pretraining-aware fine-tuning strategies.\n175\t\n176\t## Key Numerical Benchmarks (unchanged from A+)\n177\t\n178\t### Cross-Instruction Probe (C1 + C2 核心实验)\n179\t\n180\t| Condition | L0 | L1 | L2 | L5 | L8 | L16 | L24 | L31 |\n181\t|-----------|----|----|----|----|----|----|-----|-----|\n182\t| Trained last_preaction | 10% | 99.6% | 100% | 100% | 100% | 100% | 100% | 100% |\n183\t| **Llama-2 base last_preaction** | **10%** | **80.2%** | **98.7%** | **100%** | **100%** | **100%** | **100%** | **100%** |\n184\t| Untrained last_preaction | 10% | 100% | 100% | 99.x% | 98.6% | 92.3% | 86.4% | 82.0% |\n185\t| Trained image_mean | 10% | — | — | — | 10% | 10% | 10% | 9.6% |\n186\t| DINOv2 | 10% | — | — | — | — | — | — | — |\n187\t\n188\tLOOCV (10-fold): Trained 100.00±0.00 (L8-L31), Untrained 96.64±7.07 → 84.76±11.59\n189\t\n190\t### L1 Attention Pattern (C2 mechanistic evidence — three-condition)\n191\t\n192\t| Metric | Untrained | Llama-2 Base | VLA Trained |\n193\t|--------|-----------|--------------|-------------|\n194\t| Attention to text/instruction | 11.7% | 36.5% | 57.7% |\n195\t| Attention to image | 87.8% | 61.7% | 21.3% |\n196\t| Instruction-dominant heads (>50%) | 0/32 | 9/32 | 24/32 |\n197\t\n198\t### Training Effect Size Summary\n199\t\n200\t| Metric | Trained | Untrained | Δ |\n201\t|--------|---------|-----------|---|\n202\t| RSA peak (image_mean) | 0.628 (L12) | 0.612 (L0) | +0.017 |\n203\t| R² peak (last_preaction) | 0.678 (L13) | 0.609 (L32) | +0.069 |\n204\t| Inst. routing L31 | 100% | 82% | +18pp |\n205\t| Inst. attention L1 | 58% | 12% | +46pp |\n206\t| Progress classification | 86.3% (L20) | 85.3% (L4) | +1pp |\n207\t\n208\t### Cross-Encoder RSA (C3)\n209\t\n210\t| Source | RSA |\n211\t|--------|-----|\n212\t| DINO cls_token | 0.692 |\n213\t| DINO patch_mean | 0.631 |\n214\t| SigLIP+Projector | 0.615 |\n215\t| VLA trained peak (L12) | 0.628 |\n216\t| CLIP ViT-L | 0.557 |\n217\t\n218\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (D060 updated — Round 4 已验证)\n219\t\n220\t### RC1: \"C1 is trivial — causal mask guarantees it\" [Round 4 N1, ACCEPTED]\n221\t**Response**: We accept this. Paper now explicitly acknowledges causal mask as structural source. C1 is repositioned as methodological framework + empirical verification, not novel finding. The framework itself (factorial design + 4 methods) has reusable value for VLA analysis.\n222\t\n223\t### RC2: \"RSA inverted-U is metric-dependent, CKA reverses\" [Round 4 N2, PARTIALLY ACCEPTED]\n224\t**Response**: Rise phase (Δρ=+0.016) acknowledged as small and qualified with CI. CKA divergence discussed in main text, not just appendix. Decline phase (Δρ=-0.206) is robust across metrics. DINOv2 ranking qualified with \"under RSA\". C3 downgraded from core claim to observation.\n225\t\n226\t### RC3: \"Ablation 5 demos underfitting\" [Round 4 N3, NO LONGER APPLICABLE]\n227\t**Response**: This concern applied to the original RSA probing analysis (MVP phase). The current paper uses entirely different analysis methods (R² action probes with MLP, counterfactual perturbation with Cohen's d, L1 attention profiling) with adequate data volumes (10 tasks × 50 timesteps × 10 demos per condition, MCCV n=1000). The 5-demo underfitting confound does not apply to the current framework.\n228\t\n229\t### RC4: \"Only tested on one VLA (OpenVLA)\" [D088-D094: NOW ADDRESSED]\n230\t**Response**: Now validated across three VLA architectures with different backbones:\n231\t- **OpenVLA** (Llama-2-7B, 32L, MHA) — 4 LIBERO suites\n232\t- **TraceVLA** (Phi-3-mini, 32L, MHA) — 4 LIBERO suites\n233\t- **NORA** (Qwen2.5-VL-3B, 36L, GQA 16h/2kv) — 2 LIBERO suites (Goal, Spatial; no Object/Long checkpoints)\n234\tCore finding (R² exit collapse, CF sensitivity) confirmed architecture-independent. L1 head count shown to be base-model-dependent (D090), strengthening the paper by distinguishing what training creates vs what it inherits. 10/12 possible matrix cells filled.\n235\t\n236\t### RC5: \"Practical implications speculative / frozen encoder confound\" [Round 4 W4]\n237\t**Response**: Encoder ranking qualified with \"under RSA\" and \"within fixed encoder configuration.\" Discussion adds explicit caveat that claims about encoder quality require across-encoder experiments. Routing optimization remains well-supported by three-condition gradient.\n238\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49e11fde-ca39-4b97-b0e5-e979be22c1ed","uuid":"a1b3f7a9-e380-48f2-af8a-a1ce4475bae5","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:10:21.893Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260527T022433/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — vla-ssd (D060 Reframe → D095 Cross-Architecture Upgrade)\n\n> D048: PI 批准按最大质量重构。A+ 版本保留为 fallback (branch paper-a-plus-backup)。\n> D060: Round 4 weak reject → C1 降为框架, C2 升为唯一核心 claim, C3 降为 qualified observation。\n> D088-D094: 跨架构验证完成（OpenVLA/Llama-2, TraceVLA/Phi-3, NORA/Qwen2.5-VL × 4 LIBERO suites）。C2 从单架构观察升级为跨架构 robust finding。RC4 基本解决。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: CoRL 2026\n- Deadline: Abstract May 26, Paper May 29\n- Format: 8 pages + references\n\n## Core Insight\n\nVLA fine-tuning 的核心贡献是学习 deliberate instruction routing——**跨三种 VLA 架构（Llama-2-7B, Phi-3-mini, Qwen2.5-VL-3B）和四种任务类型一致成立**。训练将 instruction 表征从 LLM 预训练的中层处理模式 reorganize 到 entry-exit bookend 模式，同时在出口层制造 R² collapse（action-relevant information 在 exit 层被选择性丢弃）。跨架构一致性表明这是 VLA 训练的 emergent property，而非特定模型的 artifact。\n\n**两类效应区分（D090）**：\n- **Training-induced（architecture-independent）**: R² exit collapse、counterfactual sensitivity 提升 — 三架构一致\n- **Base-model-dependent（NOT training-induced）**: L1 head count — 取决于 base VLM/LLM 的预训练 attention 模式\n\n**三层级路由梯度（D094）**: VLM base（无 routing）→ OXE-pretrained VLA（通用 routing）→ task-finetuned VLA（任务特化 routing）。Routing 在 VLM→VLA 转换时 emerge，在 general→task-specific 转换时 reshape。\n\n## Core Claims (D060 重构：1 核心 + 1 框架 + 1 观察)\n\n### C1: Experimental Framework + Architecture-Verified Specialization [方法论贡献，非 empirical finding]\n**重新定位（D060）**: Token-level specialization 是 causal mask 的数学必然（image tokens 在序列中先于 instruction tokens，无法 attend to instructions）+ frozen encoder 不接收 instruction input。论文贡献不是\"发现\"这一点，而是：\n- **(a) 系统实验框架**：factorial design (trained/pretrained/untrained × instruction presence) + 四种互补分析方法（cross-instruction probe + attention + RSA + MLP probe），适用于任何 decoder-only VLA\n- **(b) 量化验证**：即使 residual stream 理论上可以 leak information，image tokens 在实际模型的全部 32 层均保持 chance（10%）。这不是 trivial——frozen encoder 权重与 LLM 权重共享 residual stream，验证了 no leakage\n- **(c) 训练差异的量化**：untrained readout L1=100% 但 L31=82%（信号衰减）vs trained 100% 全程稳定——framework 揭示了训练影响 routing robustness 而非 routing existence\n\nKey evidence (unchanged):\n- Cross-instruction probe: same frame × 10 instructions → 10-way classification\n- Dense L0-L32: image_mean = chance at ALL layers\n- LOOCV: 100%±0.00 trained, decaying untrained\n- **承认**: 10-way classification 本身 trivially easy（untrained L1 也 100%），贡献在于 framework + 三条件对比揭示的 routing 差异\n\n### C2: Three Qualitatively Different Routing Strategies — VLA Fine-tuning Achieves Immediate Dedicated Routing\n三条件揭示三种定性不同的 routing 模式：\n\n**L1 Attention Routing (heads + attention fraction):**\n- **Untrained (random init)**: 0/32 heads, 12% text attention\n- **Llama-2 base (pretrained, no VLA)**: 9/32 heads, 36.5% text attention\n- **VLA Trained**: 24/32 heads, 58% text attention\n\n**Full-Layer Probe Profile (instruction classification accuracy):**\n- **Trained**: L1=99.6% → 全程 100% — \"即时路由 + 完全稳定\"\n- **Llama-2 base**: L1=80.2% → L2=98.7% → L5+=100% — \"渐进建立 + 稳定维持\"\n- **Untrained**: L1=100% → L8=98.6% → L31=82% — \"偶然路由 + 逐渐遗忘\"\n\n**VLA Fine-tuning 的独特贡献（精��化）：**\n1. **即时性**：L1 即达 99.6%（vs pretrained 需 5 层才饱和）\n2. **头数专用化**：24/32 heads instruction-dominant（vs pretrained 9/32）\n3. **不是**深层稳定性 — 稳定性来自 pretrained weights（pretrained 也不衰减）\n\n**深层���减只发生在 random init**：说明结构化的 pretrained 表示（无论是否经过 VLA 训练）都能维持 instruction signal；random weights 的噪声累积导致信号退化。\n\n**Full 32-Layer Attention Profile（D054 升级，dense evidence）：**\n- **Untrained**: 全 32 层 × 所有 head = 0 instruction-dominant。完全无语言处理能力。\n- **Llama-2 base**: 倒U型 — L0-L4 低(0-10 heads) → L9-L16 高峰(15-22 heads) → L31 回落(8)。经典 LM pattern：中层做深度语义处理。\n- **VLA Trained**: 书挡型 — L0-L1 高峰(21-24 heads) → L2-L30 低谷(0-11) → L31 再次高峰(18)。入口获取 instruction + 出口条件化 action output。\n\n**C2 Claim（D073 reframe: open-loop functional sensitivity）**: VLA fine-tuning **shifts** instruction attention from mid-layer processing (Llama-2 base: 15-22/32 heads at L10-L17) to entry-layer routing (L0-L1: 21-24/32) and exit-layer re-engagement (L31: 18/32)。Instruction-conditioned action generation operates through **distributed L1 routing** where instruction-attention fraction predicts per-head contribution magnitude (specificity ratio 1.08x at action output)。Routing modulates output direction (d=0.65) without systematic quality degradation (ΔMSE≈0), consistent with an information-computation dissociation (Hewitt & Liang 2019)。不能 claim instruction heads \"uniquely responsible\" 或 \"confirms routing function\"——用 \"open-loop functional sensitivity\" + \"support\" 而非 \"confirm\"。可 claim \"disproportionate contribution\" + \"attention-ordered routing\"。Section 标题用 \"Open-loop functional sensitivity\"，正文用 \"shifts...from...to...\" + \"distributed routing\"。\n\nKey evidence:\n- **32-layer dense attention profile**: Trained bookend (L0-1: 21-24, L31: 18) vs Llama2base inverted-U (L9-16: 15-22)\n- Three-condition full-layer probe: trained flat 100%; llama2base saturates L5+100%; untrained decays L1:100%→L31:82%\n- L1 attention gradient: 0/32 → 9/32 → 24/32 heads\n- VLA-specific contributions: (1) temporal reorganization from mid-peak to bookend, (2) immediacy (L1: 80.2→99.6%), (3) head dedication (9→25 at L1)\n- **Per-token normalization**: 38.2x text/image ratio (trained instr-dom) vs 1.5x (untrained) — eliminates token-count confound\n- **Trajectory-level d**: all conditions d>2.0 (token-level is conservative ~4x underestimate)\n- **GT error**: ΔMSE≈0 (ablation redirects outputs without degrading GT accuracy) — supports information-computation dissociation\n- **Token overlap**: Spearman ρ=1.0 between token novelty and d — lexical/positional sensitivity, not semantic distance\n- **LOO sensitivity**: all leave-one-out p ≤ 0.083, no qualitative reversal; cream cheese reclassification p=0.008\n- **4-condition training trajectory (D075)**: untrained(0) → llama2(9) → bridge-vla(24) → libero-finetuned(22) at L1。Entry routing 稳定，但 L31 exit engagement 18→0（entry-exit → entry-only sharpening）。Probe accuracy 不变（L31 仍 100%），确认 attention-representation dissociation\n- **OXE training diversity**: openvla-7b 在 Open X-Embodiment 970K episodes（多平台多任务）上训练，L1 routing 不是 LIBERO-specific\n\n#### C2-X: Cross-Architecture Validation (D088-D094 — 论文最强升级)\n\n**三架构 × 四 suite 矩阵**验证 C2 不是 OpenVLA-specific artifact：\n\n**R² Exit Collapse（D096 修正：VLM→VLA transition effect, NOT universally architecture-independent）：**\n\n| Arch (backbone) | Suite | Trained Δ (peak−exit) | Untrained Δ | Collapse? | Note |\n|-----------------|-------|----------------------|-------------|-----------|------|\n| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Goal | 0.016 | 0.033 | ❌ | untrained(OXE) Δ更大 |\n| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Spatial | 0.037 | TBD | ❌ | v3 MCCV: below Δ>0.10 threshold |\n| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Object | 0.037 | 0.076 | ❌ | v3 MCCV: below Δ>0.10 threshold |\n| OpenVLA (Llama-2-7B) | Long (OFT) | 0.004 | 0.016 | ❌ | OFT finetuning, 两条件均平坦 |\n| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Goal | 0.228 | 0.048 | ✅ | |\n| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Spatial | 0.138 | 0.016 | ✅ | |\n| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Object | 0.294 | 0.009 | ✅ | |\n| TracVLA (Phi-3-mini) | Long | 0.198 | 0.028 | ✅ | |\n| NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B) | Goal | 0.691 | 0.044 | ✅ | 最极端 |\n| NORA (Qwen2.5-VL-3B) | Spatial | 0.302 | 0.037 | ✅ | |\n\n**D096+D099+D102 修正结论（v3 MCCV 更新）**：R² exit collapse 在 VLM→VLA 转换中 6/6 一致（TracVLA + NORA 所有 untrained 均为纯 VLM，Δ=0.156-0.455）。在 OXE-pretrained→LIBERO 转换中 0/4 cells 超过 Δ>0.10 阈值（Goal Δ=0.086, Spatial Δ=0.037, Object Δ=0.037, Long Δ=0.033）。v3 demo-level MCCV 修正了 v2 的 train-test leakage 后，OpenVLA Spatial/Object 的 Δ 从 0.110/0.121 下降至 0.037/0.037，证实 VLA→VLA 转换不产生实质性 exit collapse。\n\n**解读（D102 更新）**：Exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA 转换的 one-time reorganization effect (6/6)，在 VLA→VLA (OXE→LIBERO) 进一步 finetuning 中不再重现 (0/4)。这一二元分离比之前的 \"task-dependent\" 解读更清晰——区分因素是 transition type（VLM→VLA vs VLA→VLA），而非 task difficulty。\n\n**论文写法**：改为 \"R² exit collapse consistently emerges when VLMs are first fine-tuned into VLAs (6/6 cells across two architectures, Δ = 0.156–0.455). In contrast, when an already-pretrained VLA undergoes further task-specific fine-tuning, no cell exceeds the Δ > 0.10 threshold (0/4 OpenVLA cells, Δ = 0.033–0.086), indicating that exit collapse is a one-time reorganization associated with the VLM-to-VLA transition rather than a cumulative effect of continued training.\"\n\n**D100 NLP Finetuning Control — Exit Collapse 是 VLA-Specific**：\nLlama-2-7b-chat（同 Llama-2-7B backbone，SFT+RLHF fine-tuned）R² per-layer 全层平坦（0.1547-0.1555），Δ=0.000。对比同 backbone 的 VLM→VLA 转换：TracVLA Δ=0.156-0.294, NORA Δ=0.302-0.455。OpenVLA (VLA→VLA) Δ=0.033-0.086 同样无实质性 collapse，进一步确认 exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA 转换特有现象。\n\n**意义**：控制了架构（同 Llama-2-7B）和 fine-tuning（NLP chat 也是 fine-tuned model）两个变量后，exit collapse 仅在 VLM→VLA 转换中出现（Δ=0.156-0.455），NLP finetuning (Δ=0.000) 和 VLA→VLA finetuning (Δ=0.033-0.086) 均无。这排除了 \"exit collapse is a generic fine-tuning artifact\" 的解释，确认 exit collapse 是 VLM→VLA transition-specific 的表征重组。R² ≈ 0.155 是 noise floor（NLP 模型无 action representation，Ridge 仅拟合 between-task variance）。\n\n**论文写法**：在 exit collapse 结论后加 \"A chat-finetuned control sharing the same Llama-2-7B backbone exhibits flat R² ≈ 0.16 across all layers (Δ ≈ 0), confirming that exit collapse is specific to action-oriented training rather than an inherent consequence of transformer fine-tuning.\"\n\n**L1 Instruction-Dominant Heads（D090: base-model-dependent, NOT training-induced）：**\n\n| Arch | Suite | Trained | Untrained | 解读 |\n|------|-------|---------|-----------|------|\n| OpenVLA | Goal | 23/32 | 26/32 (OXE pretrained) | Finetuning 减少 3 头（→mixed），h13 跨条件共有 |\n| OpenVLA | Object | 24/32 | 24/32 (OXE pretrained) | OXE 已创建 routing |\n| OpenVLA | Long | 14/32 (OFT) | 25/32 (OXE) | OFT 增加 mixed heads |\n| TracVLA | All 4 suites | 27-30/32 | 32/32 | Phi-3-Vision 预训练已 32/32 全极化 |\n| NORA | Goal | 13/16 | 13/16 | Qwen2.5-VL 预训练已 13/16 |\n| NORA | Spatial | 12/16 | 14/16 | 同上 |\n\n**关键区分**: L1 head count 反映 base model 的语言预训练 attention 模式，**不是** VLA 训练效果。TracVLA untrained（纯 VLM）已 32/32，训练反而减少到 27-30/32（repurpose some heads）。**论文不能 claim L1 heads 是训练学到的**——只能 claim R² collapse 和 CF sensitivity 是训练效果。\n\n**Counterfactual Sensitivity（training-induced）：**\n\n| Arch | Suite | Trained (top d/cos) | Untrained (top d/cos) | 训练效应 |\n|------|-------|---------------------|----------------------|----------|\n| OpenVLA | Goal | d=1.18 (wrong) | d=1.05 (empty) | ✓ same metric, Δ=+0.13; wrong>empty (1.182>1.170) |\n| OpenVLA | Spatial | d=1.17 (empty) | d=0.94 (empty) | ✓ same metric, Δ=+0.23 |\n| OpenVLA | Object | d=1.21 (empty) | cos=0.569 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n| TracVLA | Goal | d=1.52 (empty) | cos=0.153 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n| TracVLA | Spatial | d=1.33 (empty) | cos=0.180 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n| TracVLA | Object | d=1.21 (empty) | cos=0.185 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n| TracVLA | Long | d=1.47 (empty) | cos=0.173 | ⚠️ incommensurable metrics |\n| NORA | Goal | cos=1.0 (saturated) | cos=0.081 | ✓ same metric, 12× |\n\n**D097+D099 修正**: TracVLA/NORA 的 trained 用 Cohen's d（action space），untrained 用 cosine distance（hidden space），两者不可比。但 OpenVLA 的 trained + untrained 均可生成 actions，可用同一 metric (Cohen's d) 公平比较。结果：trained 全面高于 untrained 但 gap 适中（Goal Δ=+0.04, Spatial Δ=+0.24），因为 OpenVLA untrained (OXE pretrained) 已是训练过的 VLA。这是唯一可做公平 trained-untrained 对比的架构。\n\n\"empty\" 在 6/8 tested trained settings 排第一（exceptions: OpenVLA Goal \"wrong\" first 1.182>1.170; OpenVLA Long \"shuffled\" first 0.565>0.505）。OpenVLA Long 整体 d 偏低（0.45-0.57），与 OFT finetuning 相关。\n\n**TracVLA Universal Mixed Heads (D091)**: h13 和 h22 在全部 4 个 LIBERO suite 的 trained 模型中一致作为 \"mixed\" head 出现（非 instruction-dominant 也非 image-dominant），而 untrained (Phi-3-Vision) 无此 pattern。暗示训练创建了功能特化的 mixed-modality heads。\n\n**Three-Tier Routing Gradient (D094)**:\n- **Tier 1 — VLM base (无 action training)**: TracVLA untrained (Phi-3-Vision) / NORA untrained (Qwen2.5-VL) — 无 R² collapse，无 CF sensitivity（cos < 0.2），L1 heads 来自语言预训练\n- **Tier 2 — OXE-pretrained VLA (通用 action training)**: OpenVLA untrained (openvla-7b, 970K OXE episodes) — 已有强 L1 routing (25/32)，强 CF (d=1.048)，无 exit collapse\n- **Tier 3 — Task-finetuned VLA**: TracVLA/NORA trained — R² exit collapse (Δ=0.156-0.455) + task-specific CF pattern。OpenVLA trained (VLA→VLA) 无额外 exit collapse (Δ=0.033-0.086)，但有 CF sharpening\n\n**论文 story 升级**: 从 \"VLA training creates routing\" 升级为 \"routing emerges at VLM→VLA transition and reshapes at general→task-specific transition\"。\n\n### C3: Vision Encoder Geometry Observation [降为 qualified observation，非 core claim]\n**重新定位（D060）**: RSA inverted-U 的 rise phase 极小（Δρ=0.016, CI 待补），CKA 完全反转 RSA ordering（untrained > trained > DINOv2），\"non-monotonic refinement\" 仅在 RSA 下成立。DINOv2 ranking 在 CKA 下不成立（CKA 中 DINOv2 排名最低）。\n\n**保留为 observation 的理由**：\n- **Decline phase 也是 RSA-specific**：L12→L32 Δρ=-0.206 远大于 rise phase，但 CKA 单调递增无 decline。不能 claim decline 是 metric-robust。\n- **R² inverted-U 是 metric-independent 的**：functional probe 确认 L8-L13 peak（0.655-0.678），之后下降。这是 C3 最强的 evidence，不依赖 RSA/CKA 选择。\n- **Metric divergence 本身是 honest observation**：\"non-monotonic under RSA, monotonic under CKA\"\n- **DINOv2 RSA ranking**：在 RSA 下 robust，但必须加 \"under RSA\" qualifier\n\n**写法要求**：\n- Abstract/Intro 中\"non-monotonic refinement\"加 \"under RSA\" qualifier\n- DINOv2 \"highest geometric foundation\" 加 \"as measured by RSA\"\n- best-vs-best Δ=+0.017 明确标 n.s.（CI includes 0）\n- Discussion 加 metric-dependence caveat（CKA 反转在正文中 qualify，不只在 appendix）\n\nKey evidence (unchanged but qualified):\n- Cross-encoder RSA table — **加 \"under RSA\" qualifier**\n- Per-layer RSA + R² profiles — **rise phase CI 待补报**\n- Cross-benchmark replication — still holds\n- **CKA divergence** — 必须在正文 acknowledge\n\n## Story Spine (D095 Cross-Architecture Upgrade)\n\n- **Problem**: VLAs fine-tune LLMs on robot data, but how training reshapes instruction routing and information integration at the token level remains uncharacterized — and whether these effects generalize across architectures is unknown.\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Prior behavioral studies (Grant et al. 2026, Haon et al. 2025) found visual dominance and instruction underutilization, but did not decompose the representational roles of different token positions, explain how training reshapes information flow, or test generalization across VLA families.\n- **Our framing**: We provide a systematic experimental framework for token-level analysis of VLAs, validated across three architectures (Llama-2-7B, Phi-3-mini, Qwen2.5-VL-3B) and four task suites. We find two consistent cross-architecture training effects: (1) trained VLAs exhibit substantial counterfactual sensitivity to instruction perturbation (Cohen's d ≥ 0.45), though metric incomparability with untrained baselines precludes quantifying the amplification; (2) R² exit collapse emerges consistently when VLMs are first fine-tuned into VLAs (6/6 cells, Δ=0.156-0.455), but does not appear in VLA-to-VLA fine-tuning (0/4 cells, Δ=0.033-0.086). A three-tier routing gradient (VLM base → general VLA → task-specific VLA) reveals that routing reorganization is a staged process.\n- **Headline results**: (1) [Framework] Systematic token-level analysis framework applicable to any decoder-only VLA, validated on 3 architectures × 4 task suites (10 cells). (2) [Core finding — CF sensitivity] Counterfactual sensitivity consistently present in trained VLAs (Cohen's d ≥ 0.45 across two architectures and eight suite combinations); metric incomparability between trained (action MSE) and untrained (cosine distance) conditions precludes quantifying the gap as a single ratio. (3) [Core finding — R² exit collapse] Collapse emerges at VLM→VLA transition (6/6 TracVLA+NORA cells, Δ=0.156-0.455) but not at VLA→VLA transition (0/4 OpenVLA cells, Δ=0.033-0.086) — one-time reorganization at VLM→VLA boundary. (4) [Core finding — routing gradient] Three-tier gradient: VLM base → OXE-pretrained VLA (general routing) → task-finetuned (task-specific, with CF sharpening). (5) [Nuance — D090] L1 head count is base-model-dependent (Phi-3 32/32 both conditions), not training-induced. (6) [Observation] Under RSA, vision encoder geometry follows inverted-U; functional probes confirm L8-L13 peak.\n- **Practical implications**: (1) VLA architecture design should optimize entry-exit instruction routing. (2) R² exit collapse is a diagnostic signature of initial VLA training — its presence/absence reveals the pretraining stage. (3) The routing gradient suggests pretraining-aware fine-tuning strategies.\n\n## Key Numerical Benchmarks (unchanged from A+)\n\n### Cross-Instruction Probe (C1 + C2 核心实验)\n\n| Condition | L0 | L1 | L2 | L5 | L8 | L16 | L24 | L31 |\n|-----------|----|----|----|----|----|----|-----|-----|\n| Trained last_preaction | 10% | 99.6% | 100% | 100% | 100% | 100% | 100% | 100% |\n| **Llama-2 base last_preaction** | **10%** | **80.2%** | **98.7%** | **100%** | **100%** | **100%** | **100%** | **100%** |\n| Untrained last_preaction | 10% | 100% | 100% | 99.x% | 98.6% | 92.3% | 86.4% | 82.0% |\n| Trained image_mean | 10% | — | — | — | 10% | 10% | 10% | 9.6% |\n| DINOv2 | 10% | — | — | — | — | — | — | — |\n\nLOOCV (10-fold): Trained 100.00±0.00 (L8-L31), Untrained 96.64±7.07 → 84.76±11.59\n\n### L1 Attention Pattern (C2 mechanistic evidence — three-condition)\n\n| Metric | Untrained | Llama-2 Base | VLA Trained |\n|--------|-----------|--------------|-------------|\n| Attention to text/instruction | 11.7% | 36.5% | 57.7% |\n| Attention to image | 87.8% | 61.7% | 21.3% |\n| Instruction-dominant heads (>50%) | 0/32 | 9/32 | 24/32 |\n\n### Training Effect Size Summary\n\n| Metric | Trained | Untrained | Δ |\n|--------|---------|-----------|---|\n| RSA peak (image_mean) | 0.628 (L12) | 0.612 (L0) | +0.017 |\n| R² peak (last_preaction) | 0.678 (L13) | 0.609 (L32) | +0.069 |\n| Inst. routing L31 | 100% | 82% | +18pp |\n| Inst. attention L1 | 58% | 12% | +46pp |\n| Progress classification | 86.3% (L20) | 85.3% (L4) | +1pp |\n\n### Cross-Encoder RSA (C3)\n\n| Source | RSA |\n|--------|-----|\n| DINO cls_token | 0.692 |\n| DINO patch_mean | 0.631 |\n| SigLIP+Projector | 0.615 |\n| VLA trained peak (L12) | 0.628 |\n| CLIP ViT-L | 0.557 |\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (D060 updated — Round 4 已验证)\n\n### RC1: \"C1 is trivial — causal mask guarantees it\" [Round 4 N1, ACCEPTED]\n**Response**: We accept this. Paper now explicitly acknowledges causal mask as structural source. C1 is repositioned as methodological framework + empirical verification, not novel finding. The framework itself (factorial design + 4 methods) has reusable value for VLA analysis.\n\n### RC2: \"RSA inverted-U is metric-dependent, CKA reverses\" [Round 4 N2, PARTIALLY ACCEPTED]\n**Response**: Rise phase (Δρ=+0.016) acknowledged as small and qualified with CI. CKA divergence discussed in main text, not just appendix. Decline phase (Δρ=-0.206) is robust across metrics. DINOv2 ranking qualified with \"under RSA\". C3 downgraded from core claim to observation.\n\n### RC3: \"Ablation 5 demos underfitting\" [Round 4 N3, NO LONGER APPLICABLE]\n**Response**: This concern applied to the original RSA probing analysis (MVP phase). The current paper uses entirely different analysis methods (R² action probes with MLP, counterfactual perturbation with Cohen's d, L1 attention profiling) with adequate data volumes (10 tasks × 50 timesteps × 10 demos per condition, MCCV n=1000). The 5-demo underfitting confound does not apply to the current framework.\n\n### RC4: \"Only tested on one VLA (OpenVLA)\" [D088-D094: NOW ADDRESSED]\n**Response**: Now validated across three VLA architectures with different backbones:\n- **OpenVLA** (Llama-2-7B, 32L, MHA) — 4 LIBERO suites\n- **TraceVLA** (Phi-3-mini, 32L, MHA) — 4 LIBERO suites\n- **NORA** (Qwen2.5-VL-3B, 36L, GQA 16h/2kv) — 2 LIBERO suites (Goal, Spatial; no Object/Long checkpoints)\nCore finding (R² exit collapse, CF sensitivity) confirmed architecture-independent. L1 head count shown to be base-model-dependent (D090), strengthening the paper by distinguishing what training creates vs what it inherits. 10/12 possible matrix cells filled.\n\n### RC5: \"Practical implications speculative / frozen encoder confound\" [Round 4 W4]\n**Response**: Encoder ranking qualified with \"under RSA\" and \"within fixed encoder configuration.\" Discussion adds explicit caveat that claims about encoder quality require across-encoder experiments. Routing optimization remains well-supported by three-condition gradient.\n","numLines":238,"startLine":1,"totalLines":238}}}
